WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Support us and become VIP member 
to remove all ads from www.OpenSubtitles.org

2
00:02:54.759 --> 00:02:58.263
Men are haunted by the vastness
of eternity.

3
00:02:59.514 --> 00:03:01.349
And so we ask ourselves...

4
00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:05.311
...will our actions echo
across the centuries?

5
00:03:06.187 --> 00:03:10.275
Will strangers hear our names
long after we 're gone...

6
00:03:10.608 --> 00:03:12.610
...and wonder who we were...

7
00:03:12.944 --> 00:03:14.946
...how bravely we fought...

8
00:03:15.989 --> 00:03:17.991
...how fiercely we loved?

9
00:04:38.446 --> 00:04:39.656
Good day for the crows.

10
00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:45.203
I told you yesterday
and I'll tell you again today.

11
00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:47.872
Remove your army from my land.

12
00:04:48.039 --> 00:04:49.874
I like your land.

13
00:04:50.458 --> 00:04:53.544
I think we'll stay. I like your soldiers too.

14
00:04:54.295 --> 00:04:55.922
They fought bravely yesterday.

15
00:04:56.089 --> 00:04:58.424
Not well. but bravely.

16
00:04:58.675 --> 00:05:00.176
They won't fight for you.

17
00:05:00.385 --> 00:05:02.387
That's what the Messenians said.

18
00:05:02.553 --> 00:05:05.515
And the Arcadians and the Epeians.

19
00:05:05.682 --> 00:05:08.726
Now they all fight for me.

20
00:05:08.893 --> 00:05:11.396
You can't have the whole world.
Agamemnon.

21
00:05:11.562 --> 00:05:13.898
It's too big. even for you.

22
00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:16.734
I don't want to watch another massacre.

23
00:05:17.068 --> 00:05:22.031
Let's settle this war in the old manner.
Your best fighter against my best.

24
00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:26.703
And if my man wins?

25
00:05:26.869 --> 00:05:28.871
We'll leave Thessaly for good.

26
00:05:29.414 --> 00:05:31.082
I'm a generous man.

27
00:05:31.249 --> 00:05:34.002
If mine wins.
you can keep your throne...

28
00:05:34.544 --> 00:05:37.130
...but Thessaly falls
under my command...

29
00:05:37.296 --> 00:05:40.550
...to fight with me whenever I call.

30
00:05:44.178 --> 00:05:46.180
Boagrius!

31
00:06:03.531 --> 00:06:05.033
This is my man.

32
00:06:07.869 --> 00:06:10.204
Achilles!

33
00:06:18.713 --> 00:06:21.174
Boagrius has this effect on many heroes.

34
00:06:22.633 --> 00:06:24.469
Careful who you insult. old king.

35
00:06:28.014 --> 00:06:31.059
My king. Achilles is not with the army.

36
00:06:31.225 --> 00:06:33.978
-Where is he?
-I sent a boy to look for him.

37
00:07:11.182 --> 00:07:13.267
I was having a good dream.

38
00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:17.188
Very good dream.

39
00:07:18.106 --> 00:07:21.818
King Agamemnon sent me. He needs to--

40
00:07:21.984 --> 00:07:24.112
I'll speak to your king in the morning.

41
00:07:24.278 --> 00:07:27.198
But my lord. it is morning.

42
00:07:28.825 --> 00:07:31.035
They're waiting for you.

43
00:07:45.842 --> 00:07:48.094
Are the stories about you true?

44
00:07:49.929 --> 00:07:52.723
They say your mother is
an immortal goddess.

45
00:07:54.433 --> 00:07:56.018
They say you can't be killed.

46
00:07:56.185 --> 00:07:59.063
I wouldn't be bothering
with the shield then. would I?

47
00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:01.566
The Thessalonian you're fighting...

48
00:08:01.732 --> 00:08:06.070
...he's the biggest man I've ever seen.
I wouldn't want to fight him.

49
00:08:08.364 --> 00:08:10.992
That's why no one will remember
your name.

50
00:08:18.708 --> 00:08:26.007
Achilles! Achilles! Achilles!

51
00:08:35.725 --> 00:08:39.228
Perhaps we should have our war tomorrow.
when you're better rested.

52
00:08:39.395 --> 00:08:41.939
I should have you whipped
for your impudence!

53
00:08:44.317 --> 00:08:45.860
Perhaps you should fight him.

54
00:08:46.319 --> 00:08:47.987
Achilles.

55
00:08:48.738 --> 00:08:50.573
Achilles.

56
00:08:52.283 --> 00:08:56.120
Look at the men's faces.
You can save hundreds of them.

57
00:08:57.663 --> 00:09:01.000
You can end this war
with a swing of your sword.

58
00:09:02.084 --> 00:09:05.671
Think how many songs they'll sing
in your honor.

59
00:09:06.589 --> 00:09:08.799
Let them go home to their wives.

60
00:09:14.597 --> 00:09:19.268
Imagine a king who fights his own battles.
Wouldn't that be a sight.

61
00:09:22.480 --> 00:09:27.401
Of all the warlords loved by the gods.
I hate him the most.

62
00:09:28.694 --> 00:09:30.863
We need him. my king.

63
00:09:31.697 --> 00:09:33.574
For now.

64
00:10:26.294 --> 00:10:28.212
Is there no one else?

65
00:10:33.718 --> 00:10:35.469
Is there no one else?

66
00:10:40.474 --> 00:10:42.101
Who are you. soldier?

67
00:10:43.102 --> 00:10:46.063
Achilles. Son of Peleus.

68
00:10:46.981 --> 00:10:48.316
Achilles?

69
00:10:49.066 --> 00:10:50.901
I'll remember the name.

70
00:10:52.069 --> 00:10:55.448
The ruler of Thessaly carries this scepter.

71
00:10:57.241 --> 00:10:58.576
Give it to your king.

72
00:11:00.161 --> 00:11:01.704
He's not my king.

73
00:11:20.806 --> 00:11:23.351
-Brothers in arms!
-Brothers in arms!

74
00:11:23.517 --> 00:11:25.728
-Friendship!
-Friendship!

75
00:11:33.361 --> 00:11:36.697
Princes of Troy.
on our last night together...

76
00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.325
...Queen Helen and I salute you.

77
00:11:42.119 --> 00:11:44.455
We've had our conflicts before. it's true.

78
00:11:45.122 --> 00:11:48.334
We fought many battles. Sparta and Troy.
And fought well!

79
00:11:50.586 --> 00:11:52.963
But I have always respected your father.

80
00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:55.716
Priam is a good king. a good man.

81
00:11:55.883 --> 00:11:59.929
I respected him as an adversary.
I respect him now as my ally.

82
00:12:01.138 --> 00:12:03.891
Hector. Paris. young princes. come.
Stand.

83
00:12:04.433 --> 00:12:05.768
Drink with me.

84
00:12:08.396 --> 00:12:09.730
Let us drink to peace.

85
00:12:10.564 --> 00:12:14.151
To peace between Troy and Sparta.

86
00:12:15.653 --> 00:12:19.657
May the gods keep the wolves in the hills
and the women in our beds.

87
00:12:43.806 --> 00:12:46.142
-For the gods.
-For the gods.

88
00:12:47.977 --> 00:12:50.771
Strong arm.
Thank the gods we made peace.

89
00:12:50.938 --> 00:12:54.483
I've seen too many of my men struck down
with this arm.

90
00:12:54.650 --> 00:12:55.776
Never again. I hope.

91
00:12:56.944 --> 00:12:59.864
Only one man wields a sword
better than you.

92
00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:01.031
Achilles.

93
00:13:01.198 --> 00:13:02.366
That madman.

94
00:13:02.533 --> 00:13:07.413
He would hurl a spear at Zeus himself.
If the god insulted him.

95
00:13:10.374 --> 00:13:14.253
See that one over there?
I picked her special for you.

96
00:13:14.587 --> 00:13:17.798
She's a little lioness.

97
00:13:19.175 --> 00:13:22.887
Thank you.
My wife waits for me in Troy.

98
00:13:24.013 --> 00:13:26.599
My wife waits for me right there.

99
00:13:26.765 --> 00:13:28.058
Wives are for breeding.

100
00:13:28.225 --> 00:13:32.062
You understand. for making little princes.
Come enjoy yourself tonight.

101
00:13:33.856 --> 00:13:36.525
You make excellent wine in Sparta.

102
00:14:26.909 --> 00:14:28.702
You shouldn't be here.

103
00:14:32.915 --> 00:14:35.292
That's what you said last night.

104
00:14:36.252 --> 00:14:38.420
Last night was a mistake.

105
00:14:40.756 --> 00:14:42.633
And the night before?

106
00:14:43.717 --> 00:14:46.220
I've made many mistakes this week.

107
00:15:01.819 --> 00:15:04.113
Do you want me to go?

108
00:15:07.908 --> 00:15:09.660
Yes.

109
00:15:20.462 --> 00:15:22.339
Where should I go?

110
00:15:23.674 --> 00:15:25.259
Away.

111
00:15:26.969 --> 00:15:28.679
Far away.

112
00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:27.112
I have something for you.

113
00:16:34.662 --> 00:16:36.580
Pearls from the Sea of Propontis.

114
00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:49.510
They're beautiful.

115
00:16:51.345 --> 00:16:53.180
But I can't wear them.

116
00:16:54.223 --> 00:16:56.517
Menelaus would kill us both.

117
00:16:58.602 --> 00:17:00.437
Don't be afraid of him.

118
00:17:01.522 --> 00:17:03.691
I'm not afraid of dying.

119
00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:08.696
I'm afraid of tomorrow.

120
00:17:12.032 --> 00:17:16.120
I'm afraid of watching you sail away
and knowing you'll never come back.

121
00:17:20.833 --> 00:17:24.920
Before you came to Sparta. I was a ghost.

122
00:17:26.505 --> 00:17:29.675
I walked. and I ate.
and I swam in the sea...

123
00:17:30.801 --> 00:17:32.970
...but I was just a ghost.

124
00:17:33.387 --> 00:17:35.139
You don't have to fear tomorrow.

125
00:17:39.643 --> 00:17:41.437
Come with me.

126
00:17:49.486 --> 00:17:52.114
Don't play with me. Don't play.

127
00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:56.535
If you come. we'll never be safe.

128
00:17:57.286 --> 00:18:00.581
Men will hunt us. the gods will curse us.

129
00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:03.041
But I'll love you.

130
00:18:05.335 --> 00:18:07.337
Till the day they burn my body...

131
00:18:08.255 --> 00:18:10.174
...I will love you.

132
00:18:34.740 --> 00:18:36.283
Tecton.

133
00:18:37.701 --> 00:18:40.871
Make the proper offerings to Poseidon
before we sail.

134
00:18:41.038 --> 00:18:43.207
We don't need any more widows in Troy.

135
00:18:43.707 --> 00:18:45.626
Goat or pig?

136
00:18:47.169 --> 00:18:49.046
Which does the sea god prefer?

137
00:18:50.172 --> 00:18:52.508
I'll wake the priest and ask him.

138
00:18:56.053 --> 00:18:57.095
Paris.

139
00:19:01.892 --> 00:19:05.562
We should get to bed.
We won't sleep on land again for weeks.

140
00:19:05.729 --> 00:19:08.357
I have no trouble sleeping on the seas.
brother.

141
00:19:08.524 --> 00:19:10.526
Athena sings lullabies to me.

142
00:19:12.402 --> 00:19:14.738
And who sang lullabies to you tonight?

143
00:19:15.239 --> 00:19:16.698
Tonight?

144
00:19:18.534 --> 00:19:21.411
Tonight was the fisherman's wife.

145
00:19:22.246 --> 00:19:23.747
A lovely creature.

146
00:19:24.873 --> 00:19:27.334
I hope you didn't let the fisherman
catch you.

147
00:19:28.627 --> 00:19:30.712
He was more concerned with the fish.

148
00:19:31.004 --> 00:19:33.048
You do understand why we're in Sparta.

149
00:19:33.215 --> 00:19:34.466
For peace.

150
00:19:34.633 --> 00:19:39.012
And you understand that Menelaus.
the king of Sparta. is a very powerful man.

151
00:19:39.179 --> 00:19:41.682
And that his brother Agamemnon.
the king of Mycenae...

152
00:19:41.849 --> 00:19:43.892
...commands all the Greek forces.

153
00:19:45.060 --> 00:19:47.521
What does this have to do
with the fisherman's wife?

154
00:19:47.688 --> 00:19:49.106
Pads...

155
00:19:49.273 --> 00:19:51.567
...you're my brother and I love you.

156
00:19:51.733 --> 00:19:54.236
But if you do anything
to endanger Troy...

157
00:19:54.403 --> 00:19:58.115
...I will rip your pretty face
from your pretty skull.

158
00:20:02.661 --> 00:20:04.913
Now get some sleep.

159
00:20:05.163 --> 00:20:07.457
We sail in the morning.

160
00:20:31.189 --> 00:20:35.402
A beautiful morning.
Poseidon has blessed our voyage.

161
00:20:35.986 --> 00:20:39.781
Sometimes the gods bless you in the
morning and curse you in the afternoon.

162
00:20:39.948 --> 00:20:42.910
Drop sail!

163
00:20:44.494 --> 00:20:45.996
Do you love me. brother?

164
00:20:47.539 --> 00:20:49.666
Would you protect me
against any enemy?

165
00:20:52.669 --> 00:20:54.880
The last time you spoke to me like this...

166
00:20:55.047 --> 00:20:58.383
...you were 10 years old.
and you'd just stolen Father's horse.

167
00:20:59.509 --> 00:21:00.761
What have you done now?

168
00:21:02.763 --> 00:21:04.139
I must show you something.

169
00:21:37.923 --> 00:21:39.633
-Where is she?
-Who. my king?

170
00:21:39.967 --> 00:21:44.346
I swear by the father of the gods.
I will gut you here if you don't tell me!

171
00:21:45.889 --> 00:21:47.683
My king!

172
00:21:48.475 --> 00:21:49.893
She left.

173
00:21:50.477 --> 00:21:51.728
With the Trojans.

174
00:21:56.650 --> 00:21:59.569
The fisherman here saw her
board their ship.

175
00:22:00.612 --> 00:22:02.072
The Trojans?

176
00:22:02.406 --> 00:22:04.574
With the young prince. Paris. She ....

177
00:22:11.331 --> 00:22:13.500
Get my ship ready.

178
00:22:14.960 --> 00:22:17.087
Turn us round. Back to Sparta.

179
00:22:17.254 --> 00:22:18.547
High on the sail!

180
00:22:18.714 --> 00:22:20.257
-Wait. wait.
-You fool!

181
00:22:20.424 --> 00:22:22.759
-Listen to me.
-Do you know what you've done?

182
00:22:23.051 --> 00:22:26.430
Do you know how many years our father
worked for peace?

183
00:22:26.930 --> 00:22:28.849
I love her.

184
00:22:30.225 --> 00:22:31.935
It's all a game to you. isn't it?

185
00:22:32.102 --> 00:22:35.939
You roam from town to town. bedding
merchants' wives and temple mates.

186
00:22:36.106 --> 00:22:38.108
You think you know
something about love.

187
00:22:38.442 --> 00:22:42.654
What about your father's love? You spat on
him when you brought her on this ship!

188
00:22:42.821 --> 00:22:46.742
What about the love for your country?
You'd let Troy burn for this woman?

189
00:22:50.412 --> 00:22:52.664
I won't let you start a war for her.

190
00:22:52.831 --> 00:22:54.332
May I speak?

191
00:22:55.500 --> 00:22:59.588
What you're saying is true. I've wronged
you. I've wronged our father.

192
00:22:59.755 --> 00:23:02.799
If you want to take Helen
back to Sparta. so be it.

193
00:23:03.633 --> 00:23:05.343
But I go with her.

194
00:23:06.094 --> 00:23:07.763
To Sparta? They'll kill you.

195
00:23:07.929 --> 00:23:10.265
Then I'll die fighting.

196
00:23:10.474 --> 00:23:14.019
Oh. and that sounds heroic to you.
doesn't it? To die fighting.

197
00:23:14.186 --> 00:23:17.189
-Little brother. have you ever killed a man?
-No.

198
00:23:17.355 --> 00:23:19.399
-Ever seen a man die in combat?
-No.

199
00:23:19.608 --> 00:23:23.820
I've killed men. and I've heard them dying.
And I've watched them dying.

200
00:23:23.987 --> 00:23:26.823
And there’s nothing glorious about it.
Nothing poetic.

201
00:23:26.990 --> 00:23:30.243
You say you want to die for love.
You know nothing about dying.

202
00:23:30.452 --> 00:23:32.621
And you know nothing about love!

203
00:23:32.788 --> 00:23:35.665
All the same. I go with her.

204
00:23:36.166 --> 00:23:38.043
I won't ask you to fight my war.

205
00:23:41.338 --> 00:23:43.090
You already have.

206
00:23:45.133 --> 00:23:46.593
To Troy!

207
00:23:46.760 --> 00:23:49.805
About ship! Set sail!

208
00:24:22.170 --> 00:24:25.590
-I want her back.
-Well. of course you do.

209
00:24:25.757 --> 00:24:27.300
She's a beautiful woman.

210
00:24:27.509 --> 00:24:31.054
I want her back so I can kill her
with my own two hands.

211
00:24:31.596 --> 00:24:34.599
I won't rest till I've burned Troy
to the ground.

212
00:24:34.766 --> 00:24:36.852
I thought you wanted peace with Troy.

213
00:24:37.394 --> 00:24:38.895
I should have listened to you.

214
00:24:39.062 --> 00:24:41.356
Peace is for the women...

215
00:24:41.857 --> 00:24:43.733
...and the weak.

216
00:24:44.734 --> 00:24:48.238
Empires are forged by war.

217
00:24:49.906 --> 00:24:53.702
All my life. I've stood by your side.
fought your enemies.

218
00:24:54.411 --> 00:24:57.914
You're the elder. you reap the glory.
This is the way of the world.

219
00:24:58.248 --> 00:25:01.710
But have I ever complained?
Have I ever asked you for anything?

220
00:25:01.877 --> 00:25:04.629
Never. You're a man of honor.

221
00:25:05.630 --> 00:25:07.507
Everyone in Greece knows this.

222
00:25:08.008 --> 00:25:10.552
The Trojans spat on my honor.

223
00:25:11.887 --> 00:25:14.681
An insult to me is an insult to you.

224
00:25:15.015 --> 00:25:19.269
And an insult to me
is an insult to all Greeks.

225
00:25:20.645 --> 00:25:22.606
Will you go to war with me. brother?

226
00:25:35.076 --> 00:25:38.246
I always thought my brother's wife
was a foolish woman...

227
00:25:38.413 --> 00:25:41.917
...but she's proved to be very useful.

228
00:25:43.710 --> 00:25:47.172
Nothing unifies a people
like a common enemy.

229
00:25:47.339 --> 00:25:49.507
The Trojans have never been conquered.

230
00:25:49.716 --> 00:25:51.801
Some say they can't be conquered.

231
00:25:53.303 --> 00:25:57.641
Old King Priam thinks he's untouchable
behind his high walls.

232
00:25:58.141 --> 00:26:01.102
He thinks the sun god will protect him.

233
00:26:01.311 --> 00:26:03.897
But the gods protect only...

234
00:26:04.814 --> 00:26:06.650
...the strong!

235
00:26:07.400 --> 00:26:09.653
If Troy falls...

236
00:26:09.945 --> 00:26:13.073
...I Control the Aegean.

237
00:26:13.240 --> 00:26:15.909
Hector commands the finest army
in the east.

238
00:26:16.076 --> 00:26:19.287
And Troy is built to withstand
a 10-year siege.

239
00:26:19.454 --> 00:26:21.831
There won't be a 10-year siege.

240
00:26:21.998 --> 00:26:25.418
I'll attack them with the greatest force
the world has ever seen.

241
00:26:25.669 --> 00:26:28.880
I want all the kings of Greece
and their armies.

242
00:26:29.506 --> 00:26:30.966
Send emissaries in the morning.

243
00:26:31.132 --> 00:26:32.384
One last thing.

244
00:26:32.550 --> 00:26:35.887
We need Achilles and his Myrmidons.

245
00:26:38.014 --> 00:26:39.516
Achilles.

246
00:26:41.893 --> 00:26:46.189
He can't be controlled.
He's as likely to fight us as the Trojans.

247
00:26:46.356 --> 00:26:49.776
We don't need to control him.
we need to unleash him.

248
00:26:50.527 --> 00:26:52.946
That man was born to end lives.

249
00:26:53.113 --> 00:26:57.534
Yes. he's a gifted killer.
But he threatens everything I've built.

250
00:26:57.784 --> 00:27:02.163
Before me. Greece was nothing.
I brought all the Greek kingdoms together.

251
00:27:02.330 --> 00:27:06.209
I created a nation out of fire worshipers
and snake eaters!

252
00:27:06.376 --> 00:27:09.129
I build the future. Nestor. Me!

253
00:27:11.214 --> 00:27:13.383
Achilles is the past.

254
00:27:13.550 --> 00:27:17.887
A man who fights for no flag.
A man loyal to no country.

255
00:27:18.054 --> 00:27:21.599
How many battles have we won
off the edge of his sword?

256
00:27:21.766 --> 00:27:25.020
This will be the greatest war
the world has ever seen.

257
00:27:25.186 --> 00:27:27.605
We need the greatest warrior.

258
00:27:32.569 --> 00:27:35.071
There's only one man he’ll listen to.

259
00:27:35.905 --> 00:27:37.741
I'll send a ship in the morning.

260
00:27:49.627 --> 00:27:50.795
Greetings. brother.

261
00:27:50.962 --> 00:27:54.841
We were told
King Odysseus is hid in the hills.

262
00:27:55.508 --> 00:27:57.260
Odysseus?

263
00:27:59.512 --> 00:28:03.141
That old bastard drinks my wine
and never pays.

264
00:28:03.892 --> 00:28:07.062
You ought to respect your king. friend.

265
00:28:07.228 --> 00:28:08.897
Respect him?

266
00:28:09.064 --> 00:28:11.274
I'd like to punch him in the face.

267
00:28:11.441 --> 00:28:14.402
He's always pawing at my wife.
trying to tear her clothes off.

268
00:28:21.743 --> 00:28:25.121
I hope Agamemnon's generals
are smarter than his emissaries.

269
00:28:30.543 --> 00:28:31.961
What did you say?

270
00:28:35.465 --> 00:28:37.675
You want me
to help you fight the Trojans.

271
00:28:44.140 --> 00:28:45.683
You're ....

272
00:28:46.684 --> 00:28:48.144
Are you...?

273
00:28:52.065 --> 00:28:55.276
Forgive us. King Odysseus.

274
00:28:59.364 --> 00:29:00.782
Well ....

275
00:29:01.449 --> 00:29:03.201
I'm gonna miss my dog.

276
00:29:03.827 --> 00:29:06.913
King Agamemnon has a favor
to ask of you.

277
00:29:08.873 --> 00:29:10.792
Of course he does.

278
00:29:36.609 --> 00:29:38.236
Never hesitate.

279
00:29:55.128 --> 00:29:56.963
Fancy Swordplay.

280
00:30:00.592 --> 00:30:02.385
Nervous?

281
00:30:04.804 --> 00:30:06.806
Petrified.

282
00:30:08.224 --> 00:30:10.977
You told me never
to change sword hands.

283
00:30:11.561 --> 00:30:16.024
Yes. When you know how to use it.
you won't be taking my orders.

284
00:30:34.584 --> 00:30:38.421
Your reputation for hospitality
is fast becoming legend.

285
00:30:44.636 --> 00:30:46.721
Patroclus. my cousin.

286
00:30:47.096 --> 00:30:49.933
Odysseus. King of Ithaca.

287
00:30:50.308 --> 00:30:52.101
Patroclus.

288
00:30:53.937 --> 00:30:55.563
I knew your parents well.

289
00:30:55.730 --> 00:30:57.357
I miss them.

290
00:30:59.734 --> 00:31:02.779
Now you have this one
watching over you. eh?

291
00:31:02.946 --> 00:31:05.156
Learning from Achilles himself.

292
00:31:06.199 --> 00:31:08.159
Kings would kill for the honor.

293
00:31:08.368 --> 00:31:10.954
Are you here at Agamemnon's bidding?

294
00:31:13.414 --> 00:31:14.791
We need to talk.

295
00:31:18.795 --> 00:31:20.797
I will not fight for him.

296
00:31:21.172 --> 00:31:23.925
I'm not asking you to fight for him.

297
00:31:24.092 --> 00:31:26.177
I'm asking you to fight for Greece.

298
00:31:26.469 --> 00:31:28.638
Have the Greeks tired of fighting
each other?

299
00:31:28.972 --> 00:31:31.641
-For now.
-For the Greeks!

300
00:31:32.767 --> 00:31:34.978
The Trojans never harmed me.

301
00:31:35.144 --> 00:31:37.230
They insulted Greece.

302
00:31:37.397 --> 00:31:41.234
They insulted a man who couldn't hold
on to his wife. Is that my business?

303
00:31:41.401 --> 00:31:44.028
Your business is war. my friend.

304
00:31:44.195 --> 00:31:47.407
Is it? Am I the whore of the battlefield?

305
00:31:48.116 --> 00:31:50.076
The man has no honor.

306
00:31:50.660 --> 00:31:52.912
I won't be remembered
as a tyrant's mercenary.

307
00:31:53.079 --> 00:31:56.666
Let Achilles fight for honor.
Let Agamemnon fight for power.

308
00:31:56.833 --> 00:32:00.086
And let the gods decide
which man to glorify.

309
00:32:01.421 --> 00:32:03.339
Forget Agamemnon.

310
00:32:03.548 --> 00:32:05.049
Fight for me.

311
00:32:05.466 --> 00:32:08.886
My wife will feel much better
if she knows you're by my side.

312
00:32:09.053 --> 00:32:11.139
I'll feel much better.

313
00:32:11.806 --> 00:32:14.434
Is Ajax going to fight in Troy?

314
00:32:14.601 --> 00:32:18.438
They say he can fell an oak tree
with one swing of the ax.

315
00:32:20.398 --> 00:32:22.233
Trees don't swing back.

316
00:32:25.445 --> 00:32:27.947
We're sending the largest fleet
that ever sailed.

317
00:32:29.532 --> 00:32:31.284
A thousand ships.

318
00:32:32.410 --> 00:32:34.037
A thousand ships?

319
00:32:34.537 --> 00:32:37.165
Prince Hector. Is he as good a warrior
as they say?

320
00:32:37.540 --> 00:32:40.543
The best of all the Trojans.

321
00:32:40.710 --> 00:32:43.963
Some say he's better
than all the Greeks too.

322
00:32:45.632 --> 00:32:47.634
Even if your cousin doesn't come...

323
00:32:47.842 --> 00:32:51.387
...I hope you'll join us.
We could use a strong arm like yours.

324
00:32:52.388 --> 00:32:54.807
Play your tricks on me.
but not my cousin.

325
00:32:55.183 --> 00:32:58.895
You have your swords. I have my tricks.

326
00:32:59.354 --> 00:33:01.397
We play with the toys the gods give us.

327
00:33:03.232 --> 00:33:05.068
We sail for Troy in three days.

328
00:33:09.405 --> 00:33:12.408
This war will never be forgotten.

329
00:33:13.743 --> 00:33:16.663
Nor will the heroes who fight in it.

330
00:33:41.688 --> 00:33:45.191
They say the king of Ithaca
has a silver tongue.

331
00:33:46.776 --> 00:33:48.611
I knew they would come for you.

332
00:33:48.778 --> 00:33:51.155
Long before you were born...

333
00:33:51.322 --> 00:33:53.449
...I knew they would come.

334
00:33:58.287 --> 00:34:00.832
They want you to fight in Troy.

335
00:34:07.922 --> 00:34:10.967
I'm making you
another Seashell necklace.

336
00:34:11.759 --> 00:34:14.220
Like the ones I made you
when you were a boy.

337
00:34:14.387 --> 00:34:15.972
Do you remember?

338
00:34:23.354 --> 00:34:24.814
Mother...

339
00:34:26.649 --> 00:34:28.568
...tonight. I decide.

340
00:34:33.656 --> 00:34:36.159
If you stay in Larisa...

341
00:34:36.993 --> 00:34:38.619
...you will find peace.

342
00:34:38.786 --> 00:34:40.580
You will find a wonderful woman.

343
00:34:40.747 --> 00:34:44.500
You will have sons and daughters.
and they will have children.

344
00:34:44.667 --> 00:34:46.669
And they will love you.

345
00:34:47.336 --> 00:34:50.089
When you are gone.
they will remember you.

346
00:34:53.342 --> 00:34:57.346
But when your children are dead
and their children after them...

347
00:34:58.347 --> 00:35:00.475
...your name will be lost.

348
00:35:04.270 --> 00:35:05.646
If you go to Troy...

349
00:35:06.773 --> 00:35:09.400
...glory will be yours.

350
00:35:10.568 --> 00:35:15.114
They will write stories about your
victories for thousands of years.

351
00:35:16.199 --> 00:35:19.327
The world will remember your name.

352
00:35:21.621 --> 00:35:23.831
But if you go to Troy...

353
00:35:26.375 --> 00:35:28.753
...you will never come home.

354
00:35:30.004 --> 00:35:33.883
For your glory walks hand in hand
with your doom.

355
00:35:36.177 --> 00:35:38.554
And I shall never see you again.

356
00:35:42.308 --> 00:35:44.602
You know this to be true. Mother?

357
00:35:45.436 --> 00:35:47.438
I know this.

358
00:38:05.201 --> 00:38:07.620
-My son.
-Father.

359
00:38:12.708 --> 00:38:13.960
Paris.

360
00:38:21.801 --> 00:38:23.052
Father.

361
00:38:24.387 --> 00:38:27.348
-This is Helen.
-Helen?

362
00:38:27.807 --> 00:38:29.892
Helen of Sparta?

363
00:38:32.311 --> 00:38:33.729
Helen of Troy.

364
00:38:40.277 --> 00:38:43.406
I've heard rumors of your beauty.

365
00:38:44.907 --> 00:38:46.575
For once...

366
00:38:47.034 --> 00:38:48.995
...the gossips were right.

367
00:38:52.289 --> 00:38:53.624
Welcome.

368
00:38:55.251 --> 00:38:56.585
Thank you. good king.

369
00:38:56.752 --> 00:38:59.130
Come. you must be tired.

370
00:39:11.809 --> 00:39:13.519
Look.

371
00:39:15.312 --> 00:39:17.106
He's grown.

372
00:39:17.606 --> 00:39:19.525
He is strong.

373
00:39:19.734 --> 00:39:21.861
He's just like his father.

374
00:39:22.987 --> 00:39:25.740
-Paris!
-Briseis!

375
00:39:29.744 --> 00:39:32.913
Beloved cousin. your beauty grows
with each new moon.

376
00:39:34.582 --> 00:39:35.833
Briseis.

377
00:39:38.294 --> 00:39:39.712
A servant of Apollo now.

378
00:39:39.879 --> 00:39:44.300
The young men of Troy were devastated
when Briseis Chose the virgin robes.

379
00:39:44.467 --> 00:39:45.593
Uncle.

380
00:39:48.971 --> 00:39:52.725
I thank the gods for your safe return.

381
00:39:55.019 --> 00:39:57.980
-For the gods.
-For the gods.

382
00:39:58.147 --> 00:39:59.899
For gods.

383
00:40:14.997 --> 00:40:16.499
Father...

384
00:40:16.665 --> 00:40:19.168
...I know this is the last thing we need.

385
00:40:19.335 --> 00:40:23.839
It is the will of the gods.
Everything is in their hands.

386
00:40:24.465 --> 00:40:28.928
-But I'm surprised you let him bring her.
-If I'd let him fight Menelaus for her...

387
00:40:29.095 --> 00:40:31.972
...you'd be burning a son's body.
not welcoming a daughter.

388
00:40:32.139 --> 00:40:34.892
We could send peace envoys
to Menelaus.

389
00:40:35.059 --> 00:40:38.187
You know Menelaus.
He'd spear their heads to his gate.

390
00:40:38.354 --> 00:40:40.773
What would you have me do?

391
00:40:42.316 --> 00:40:44.735
Put her on a ship and send her home.

392
00:40:47.863 --> 00:40:50.908
Women have always loved Paris.
and he has loved them back.

393
00:40:51.075 --> 00:40:52.993
But this is different.

394
00:40:53.160 --> 00:40:55.496
Something has changed in him.

395
00:40:55.663 --> 00:40:59.458
If we send her home to Menelaus.
he will follow her.

396
00:41:00.376 --> 00:41:03.337
This is my country.
and these are my countrymen.

397
00:41:03.546 --> 00:41:07.007
I don't want to see them suffer
so my brother can have his prize.

398
00:41:07.883 --> 00:41:10.094
It's not just the Spartans
coming after her.

399
00:41:10.302 --> 00:41:12.555
By now. Menelaus has gone
to Agamemnon.

400
00:41:12.721 --> 00:41:15.558
And Agamemnon has wanted
to destroy us for years.

401
00:41:15.724 --> 00:41:18.102
Once we're out of the way.
he controls the seas.

402
00:41:18.602 --> 00:41:23.274
Enemies have been attacking us
for centuries. Our walls still stand.

403
00:41:24.024 --> 00:41:26.902
Father. we can't win this war.

404
00:41:27.778 --> 00:41:30.114
Apollo watches over us.

405
00:41:30.573 --> 00:41:33.826
Even Agamemnon is no match
for the gods.

406
00:41:33.993 --> 00:41:36.745
And how many battalions
does the sun god command?

407
00:41:36.912 --> 00:41:38.497
Do not mock the gods.

408
00:41:42.418 --> 00:41:45.921
When you were very young.
you came down with scarlet fever.

409
00:41:46.088 --> 00:41:49.216
Your little hand was so hot.

410
00:41:49.383 --> 00:41:52.636
The healer said
you would not last the night.

411
00:41:52.887 --> 00:41:58.767
I went down to Apollo's temple
and I prayed until the sun came up.

412
00:41:58.976 --> 00:42:03.230
That walk back to the palace
was the longest of my life.

413
00:42:03.397 --> 00:42:07.776
But I went into your mother's room
and you were sleeping in her arms.

414
00:42:07.943 --> 00:42:09.695
The fever had broken.

415
00:42:10.654 --> 00:42:14.450
I promised that day
to dedicate my life to the gods.

416
00:42:14.617 --> 00:42:16.619
I will not break my promise.

417
00:42:16.785 --> 00:42:21.540
For thirty years I have worked for peace.
Thirty years.

418
00:42:21.916 --> 00:42:25.002
Paris is a fool sometimes. I know that.

419
00:42:25.169 --> 00:42:29.965
But I will fight 1000 wars
before letting him die.

420
00:42:30.841 --> 00:42:34.970
Forgive me. Father.
but you won't be the one fighting.

421
00:42:54.823 --> 00:42:56.617
They're coming for me.

422
00:42:57.660 --> 00:42:59.495
The wind is bringing them closer.

423
00:42:59.662 --> 00:43:01.330
What if we left?

424
00:43:01.497 --> 00:43:04.333
Tonight. Right now.

425
00:43:04.500 --> 00:43:08.295
What if we went down to the stables.
took two horses and left?

426
00:43:08.504 --> 00:43:10.965
Ride east. keep riding.

427
00:43:11.131 --> 00:43:13.842
-And go where?
-Away from here.

428
00:43:14.343 --> 00:43:17.763
I could hunt deer. rabbit. I could feed us.

429
00:43:20.766 --> 00:43:23.185
But this is your home.

430
00:43:23.894 --> 00:43:26.313
You left your home for me.

431
00:43:30.192 --> 00:43:32.444
Sparta was never my home.

432
00:43:33.028 --> 00:43:36.365
My parents sent my there when I was 16
to marry Menelaus.

433
00:43:36.532 --> 00:43:37.992
But it was never my home.

434
00:43:38.158 --> 00:43:40.077
We'll live off the land.

435
00:43:40.244 --> 00:43:44.206
No more palaces for us. No more servants.
We don't need any of that.

436
00:43:44.373 --> 00:43:45.791
And your family?

437
00:43:45.958 --> 00:43:49.795
We'd be protecting my family. If we're
not here. what's the need for war?

438
00:43:50.004 --> 00:43:53.757
Menelaus won't give up.
He'll track us to the end of the world.

439
00:43:53.966 --> 00:43:57.845
He doesn't know these lands. I do.
We can lose ourselves in a day.

440
00:43:58.012 --> 00:43:59.888
You don't know Menelaus.

441
00:44:00.055 --> 00:44:02.182
You don't know his brother.

442
00:44:02.725 --> 00:44:06.228
They'll burn every house in Troy
to find us.

443
00:44:07.479 --> 00:44:09.982
They'll never believe we've left.

444
00:44:10.149 --> 00:44:13.902
And even if they do.
they'll burn it for spite.

445
00:44:17.114 --> 00:44:19.658
Then I'll make it easy for him to find me.

446
00:44:22.328 --> 00:44:24.955
I'll walk right up to him
and tell him you're mine.

447
00:44:34.840 --> 00:44:36.884
You're very young. my love.

448
00:44:39.470 --> 00:44:41.347
We're the same age.

449
00:44:43.682 --> 00:44:46.310
You're younger than I ever was.

450
00:48:26.488 --> 00:48:28.991
Take up your positions!

451
00:48:53.181 --> 00:48:56.351
Black sail. it's Achilles.

452
00:48:56.518 --> 00:48:57.936
What's the fool doing?

453
00:48:58.353 --> 00:49:02.024
He's going to take the beach of Troy
with 50 men?

454
00:49:05.319 --> 00:49:07.988
Row. Myrmidon. row!

455
00:49:11.199 --> 00:49:12.534
My lord?

456
00:49:14.202 --> 00:49:16.204
Should we wait for the others?

457
00:49:17.372 --> 00:49:20.375
-They brought us here for war.
-Yes. but Agamemnon's orders--

458
00:49:20.542 --> 00:49:23.045
You fight for me. Eudorus.
or Agamemnon?

459
00:49:23.211 --> 00:49:24.546
For you. my lord.

460
00:49:24.713 --> 00:49:29.134
Then fight for me. And let the servants
of Agamemnon fight for him.

461
00:49:37.684 --> 00:49:39.811
Make way there! Make way!

462
00:49:50.572 --> 00:49:53.950
Tecton. is the Apollonian Guard ready?

463
00:49:54.117 --> 00:49:57.371
-Waiting at the city gates.
-Good. I'll be right there.

464
00:49:58.246 --> 00:50:00.999
Lysander. how long
before the army is ready?

465
00:50:01.166 --> 00:50:04.294
Half of our men are still coming.
We have to arm them--

466
00:50:04.461 --> 00:50:05.962
-How long?
-Noon.

467
00:50:06.129 --> 00:50:07.798
Make it sooner.

468
00:50:07.964 --> 00:50:11.176
And Lysander. I want patrols
to scour the countryside.

469
00:50:11.343 --> 00:50:13.095
I want every home
and pasture checked...

470
00:50:13.261 --> 00:50:15.389
...every Trojan to be
brought inside the city walls.

471
00:50:15.555 --> 00:50:17.474
If they can't walk. carry them.

472
00:50:32.406 --> 00:50:34.116
Patroclus!

473
00:50:37.119 --> 00:50:38.662
Put down your spear.

474
00:50:38.829 --> 00:50:40.914
-I'm fighting the Trojans.
-Not today.

475
00:50:41.081 --> 00:50:42.999
I'm ready. You taught me how to fight.

476
00:50:43.166 --> 00:50:47.045
And you're a good student.
But you're not a Myrmidon yet.

477
00:50:48.964 --> 00:50:50.465
Look at these men.

478
00:50:50.632 --> 00:50:54.928
They are the fiercest soldiers in all
of Greece. Each of them has bled for me.

479
00:50:55.095 --> 00:50:57.097
-Guard the ship.
-But this is a war.

480
00:50:57.264 --> 00:51:01.560
Cousin. I can't fight the Trojans if I'm
concerned for you. Guard the ship.

481
00:51:22.789 --> 00:51:24.499
Trojans!

482
00:51:27.335 --> 00:51:30.255
All my life. I've lived by a code.

483
00:51:30.756 --> 00:51:32.799
And the code is simple:

484
00:51:32.966 --> 00:51:36.470
Honor the gods. love your woman...

485
00:51:36.636 --> 00:51:37.888
...and defend your country.

486
00:51:40.348 --> 00:51:42.267
Troy is mother to us all.

487
00:51:42.893 --> 00:51:44.144
Fight for her!

488
00:52:03.663 --> 00:52:04.706
Myrmidons...

489
00:52:06.416 --> 00:52:08.168
...my brothers of the sword.

490
00:52:09.586 --> 00:52:13.006
I'd rather fight beside you
than any army of thousands.

491
00:52:13.173 --> 00:52:16.551
Let no man forget now menacing we are.
We are lions!

492
00:52:20.430 --> 00:52:25.227
Do you know what's there. waiting.
beyond that beach?

493
00:52:25.393 --> 00:52:28.563
Immortality! Take it! it's yours!

494
00:52:41.576 --> 00:52:43.036
Fight positions!

495
00:52:43.203 --> 00:52:45.080
Archers!

496
00:52:45.997 --> 00:52:47.749
Archers. draw!

497
00:52:49.668 --> 00:52:51.086
Draw!

498
00:53:07.686 --> 00:53:09.396
Keep forward!

499
00:53:28.748 --> 00:53:30.333
Form up!

500
00:53:30.834 --> 00:53:32.377
Formation!

501
00:53:33.086 --> 00:53:35.213
The man wants to die.

502
00:53:55.650 --> 00:53:57.110
On my command!

503
00:54:04.951 --> 00:54:06.786
Break off! Break off!

504
00:54:31.519 --> 00:54:34.606
Achilles! Achilles! Achilles!

505
00:54:34.773 --> 00:54:36.483
Achilles! Achilles!

506
00:54:36.650 --> 00:54:42.197
Achilles! Achilles! Achilles!

507
00:54:42.364 --> 00:54:45.492
Give him the battle.
we'll take the war.

508
00:54:45.659 --> 00:54:49.829
Give him too many battles and
the men will forget who's king.

509
00:55:03.510 --> 00:55:06.429
Ajax. you need to see this.

510
00:55:08.264 --> 00:55:09.724
Look at him...

511
00:55:09.891 --> 00:55:12.602
...hogging all the glory.

512
00:55:13.728 --> 00:55:16.773
Row. you lazy whores. row!

513
00:55:17.023 --> 00:55:19.859
Greeks are dying! Row!

514
00:55:48.888 --> 00:55:52.100
Those men down there need help. Now!
Tecton. with me.

515
00:56:04.779 --> 00:56:08.116
I am Ajax. breaker of stones!

516
00:56:08.283 --> 00:56:11.161
Look upon me and despair!

517
00:56:11.745 --> 00:56:14.247
Flank! To the flank!

518
00:57:05.799 --> 00:57:07.050
No!

519
00:57:37.247 --> 00:57:39.249
Achilles! Achilles!

520
00:57:44.504 --> 00:57:47.715
Back to the City! Back to the city!

521
00:58:03.106 --> 00:58:06.776
The sun god is a patron of Troy.
our enemy.

522
00:58:07.986 --> 00:58:10.655
Take whatever treasure you can find.

523
00:58:17.912 --> 00:58:19.581
With your permission. my lord.

524
00:58:24.586 --> 00:58:27.505
-Speak.
-Apollo sees everything.

525
00:58:27.672 --> 00:58:30.466
Perhaps it is not wise to offend him.

526
00:58:54.115 --> 00:58:55.533
Warn the men.

527
00:58:56.701 --> 00:58:58.328
Wait.

528
01:00:49.897 --> 01:00:54.068
You are very brave or very stupid
to come after me alone.

529
01:00:55.903 --> 01:00:57.572
You must be Hector.

530
01:01:05.788 --> 01:01:07.749
Do you know who I am?

531
01:01:10.752 --> 01:01:12.754
These priests weren't armed.

532
01:01:14.756 --> 01:01:19.135
Yes. There's no honor
in cutting old men's throats.

533
01:01:19.635 --> 01:01:23.056
Only children and fools fight for honor.

534
01:01:23.222 --> 01:01:25.058
I fight for my country.

535
01:01:26.934 --> 01:01:28.644
Fight me!

536
01:01:35.068 --> 01:01:37.612
Why kill you now. prince of Troy...

537
01:01:37.779 --> 01:01:39.739
...with no one here to see you fall?

538
01:01:52.460 --> 01:01:54.087
Why did you come here?

539
01:01:54.587 --> 01:01:57.131
They'll be talking about this war
for 1000 years.

540
01:01:58.257 --> 01:02:01.511
In 1000 years. the dust
from our bones will be gone.

541
01:02:01.803 --> 01:02:05.056
Yes. prince. But our names will remain.

542
01:02:15.691 --> 01:02:19.695
Go home. prince. Drink some wine.
make love to your wife.

543
01:02:20.154 --> 01:02:21.906
Tomorrow. we'll have our war.

544
01:02:25.201 --> 01:02:27.578
You speak of war as if it's a game.

545
01:02:27.745 --> 01:02:31.541
How many wives wait at Troy's gates
for husbands they’ll never see again?

546
01:02:31.999 --> 01:02:36.796
Your brother can comfort them. I hear
he's good at charming other men's wives.

547
01:02:51.853 --> 01:02:53.521
My lord. you let him go?

548
01:02:56.691 --> 01:02:59.485
It's too early in the day for killing princes.

549
01:03:31.058 --> 01:03:34.187
Achilles! Achilles!

550
01:03:34.353 --> 01:03:40.276
Achilles! Achilles! Achilles!

551
01:04:14.602 --> 01:04:17.104
-Achilles.
-Ajax.

552
01:04:17.563 --> 01:04:22.151
You're as fearless as the gods.
I'm honored to go to war with you.

553
01:04:22.318 --> 01:04:23.736
As am I.

554
01:04:25.112 --> 01:04:26.989
If you sailed slower.
the war would be over.

555
01:04:27.156 --> 01:04:29.784
I'll miss the start as long as I'm here
at the end.

556
01:04:29.951 --> 01:04:31.953
My lord?

557
01:04:32.119 --> 01:04:34.330
I've got something to show you.

558
01:04:52.640 --> 01:04:55.685
The men found her hiding in the temple.

559
01:04:56.352 --> 01:04:57.770
They thought she'd...

560
01:04:58.771 --> 01:05:00.439
...amuse you.

561
01:05:11.701 --> 01:05:13.160
What's your name?

562
01:05:17.498 --> 01:05:19.166
Did you not hear me?

563
01:05:20.626 --> 01:05:22.545
You killed Apollo's priests.

564
01:05:22.712 --> 01:05:24.880
I've killed men in five Countries.
never a priest.

565
01:05:25.047 --> 01:05:27.133
Then your men did.

566
01:05:27.550 --> 01:05:29.510
The sun god will have his vengeance.

567
01:05:30.177 --> 01:05:32.013
What's he waiting for?

568
01:05:32.179 --> 01:05:34.390
The right time to strike.

569
01:05:36.976 --> 01:05:40.021
His priests are dead.
and his acolyte's a captive.

570
01:05:41.230 --> 01:05:44.734
-I think your god is afraid of me.
-Afraid?

571
01:05:45.192 --> 01:05:48.195
Apollo is master of the sun.
He fears nothing.

572
01:05:48.362 --> 01:05:51.198
-Where is he?
-You're nothing but a killer!

573
01:05:51.365 --> 01:05:54.118
You wouldn't know anything
about the gods.

574
01:05:56.871 --> 01:05:59.957
I know more about the gods
than your priests.

575
01:06:00.625 --> 01:06:02.126
I've seen them.

576
01:06:08.633 --> 01:06:10.384
You're royalty. aren't you?

577
01:06:13.220 --> 01:06:15.556
Spent years talking down to men.

578
01:06:19.727 --> 01:06:21.395
You must be royalty.

579
01:06:23.648 --> 01:06:25.066
What's your name?

580
01:06:30.863 --> 01:06:33.532
Even the servants of Apollo have names.

581
01:06:39.413 --> 01:06:41.248
Briseis.

582
01:06:44.335 --> 01:06:46.337
Are you afraid. Briseis?

583
01:06:47.421 --> 01:06:48.923
Should I be?

584
01:06:52.593 --> 01:06:54.095
My lord.

585
01:06:56.263 --> 01:06:59.016
Agamemnon requests your presence.

586
01:06:59.684 --> 01:07:02.478
The kings are gathering
to celebrate the victory.

587
01:07:04.855 --> 01:07:06.649
You fought well today.

588
01:07:08.150 --> 01:07:09.777
My lord.

589
01:07:14.824 --> 01:07:16.867
What do you want here in Troy?

590
01:07:17.827 --> 01:07:19.870
You didn't come for the Spartan queen.

591
01:07:20.037 --> 01:07:21.789
I want what all men want.

592
01:07:22.289 --> 01:07:23.958
I just want it more.

593
01:07:30.381 --> 01:07:32.466
You don't need to fear me. girl.

594
01:07:33.342 --> 01:07:35.678
You're the only Trojan who can say that.

595
01:08:19.889 --> 01:08:22.308
King Triopas. my lord.

596
01:08:24.101 --> 01:08:27.521
You have won a great victory.
my king of kings.

597
01:08:28.355 --> 01:08:32.651
No one thought the Trojan beach
could be captured so easily.

598
01:08:33.194 --> 01:08:35.529
A beautiful gift. Triopas.

599
01:08:36.280 --> 01:08:41.535
You will be among the first to walk
in the streets of Troy tomorrow.

600
01:08:45.206 --> 01:08:49.502
My father. Neleus. had this urn made to
commemorate his victory at Cyparisseis.

601
01:08:49.668 --> 01:08:51.504
I present it to you...

602
01:08:51.754 --> 01:08:54.548
...in honor of an even more
memorable victory.

603
01:08:54.799 --> 01:08:56.383
Thank you. old friend.

604
01:08:57.051 --> 01:09:00.888
Tomorrow. we'll eat supper
in the gardens of Troy.

605
01:09:09.814 --> 01:09:11.148
Leave us.

606
01:09:19.365 --> 01:09:23.911
War is young men dying and old men
talking. You know this.

607
01:09:24.078 --> 01:09:26.163
Ignore the politics.

608
01:09:43.597 --> 01:09:45.432
Apparently. you won some great victory.

609
01:09:45.599 --> 01:09:51.272
Perhaps you didn't notice. The Trojan
beach belonged to Priam in the morning.

610
01:09:51.438 --> 01:09:54.316
It belongs to Agamemnon
in the afternoon.

611
01:09:54.608 --> 01:09:56.819
Have the beach.
I didn't come here for sand.

612
01:09:56.986 --> 01:09:58.279
No.

613
01:09:58.445 --> 01:10:02.324
You came here because you want
your name to last through the ages.

614
01:10:04.743 --> 01:10:06.829
A great victory was won today.

615
01:10:08.247 --> 01:10:10.541
But that victory is not yours.

616
01:10:10.708 --> 01:10:13.127
Kings did not kneel to Achilles.

617
01:10:13.294 --> 01:10:16.088
Kings did not pay homage to Achilles.

618
01:10:16.255 --> 01:10:19.884
Perhaps the kings were too far behind
to see. Soldiers won the battle.

619
01:10:20.050 --> 01:10:22.303
History remembers kings!

620
01:10:22.803 --> 01:10:24.555
Not soldiers.

621
01:10:26.640 --> 01:10:29.226
Tomorrow. we'll batter down
the gates of Troy.

622
01:10:29.435 --> 01:10:32.146
I'll build monuments
on every island of Greece.

623
01:10:32.313 --> 01:10:35.399
I'll Carve "Agamemnon" in the stone.

624
01:10:35.566 --> 01:10:38.110
My name will last through the ages.

625
01:10:38.277 --> 01:10:41.989
Your name is written in sand...

626
01:10:42.156 --> 01:10:44.116
...for the waves to wash away.

627
01:10:44.283 --> 01:10:48.787
Be careful. king of kings.
First. you need the victory.

628
01:10:53.667 --> 01:10:56.128
Your men sacked the temple
of Apollo. yes?

629
01:10:56.337 --> 01:10:58.005
You want gold? Take it.

630
01:10:58.172 --> 01:11:01.258
It's my gift to honor your courage.
Take what you wish.

631
01:11:01.425 --> 01:11:03.344
I already have.

632
01:11:06.013 --> 01:11:07.264
Aphareus!

633
01:11:08.515 --> 01:11:09.850
Haemon!

634
01:11:20.069 --> 01:11:21.236
The spoils of war.

635
01:11:21.779 --> 01:11:25.783
No argument with you. but if you don't
release her. you'll never see home again.

636
01:11:26.200 --> 01:11:28.619
-Decide.
-Guards!

637
01:11:30.412 --> 01:11:31.997
Stop!

638
01:11:33.165 --> 01:11:35.125
Too many people have died today.

639
01:11:36.961 --> 01:11:39.964
If killing is your only talent.
that's your curse.

640
01:11:40.798 --> 01:11:43.342
I don't want anyone dying for me.

641
01:11:51.892 --> 01:11:57.856
Mighty Achilles. silenced by a slave girl.

642
01:12:01.068 --> 01:12:05.364
Tonight. I'll have her give me a bath.

643
01:12:05.990 --> 01:12:07.700
And then...

644
01:12:08.158 --> 01:12:10.619
-...who knows?
-You sack of wine!

645
01:12:12.287 --> 01:12:16.792
Before my time is done. I will look
down on your corpse and smile.

646
01:13:33.827 --> 01:13:37.790
If they want a war.
we will give them a war.

647
01:13:38.957 --> 01:13:43.712
I would match the best of Troy
against the best of Greece any day.

648
01:13:44.421 --> 01:13:48.092
The best of Greece outnumber
the best of Troy two to one.

649
01:13:48.258 --> 01:13:50.177
So. what do you suggest?

650
01:13:50.344 --> 01:13:51.970
We surrender our city?

651
01:13:52.179 --> 01:13:56.183
We allow the Greeks to slaughter our men?
Rape our wives?

652
01:13:56.350 --> 01:13:58.102
I suggest diplomacy.

653
01:13:58.268 --> 01:14:00.354
The Greeks came here for one thing.

654
01:14:00.521 --> 01:14:04.566
Let's be honest. my friends.
Trojans are now burning on the pyre...

655
01:14:05.442 --> 01:14:09.530
...because of one youthful indiscretion.

656
01:14:10.280 --> 01:14:12.032
Glaucus.

657
01:14:12.533 --> 01:14:16.286
You have fought with me for 40 years.
Can we win this war?

658
01:14:16.453 --> 01:14:19.164
Our walls have never been breached.

659
01:14:19.373 --> 01:14:21.708
We have the finest archers in the world.

660
01:14:22.209 --> 01:14:23.836
And we have Hector...

661
01:14:24.002 --> 01:14:28.549
...whose men would fight
the shades of Tartarus if he commanded.

662
01:14:28.715 --> 01:14:31.552
Yes. we can win.

663
01:14:40.811 --> 01:14:43.605
I spoke with two farmers today.

664
01:14:44.022 --> 01:14:48.944
They saw an eagle flying
with a serpent clutched in its talons.

665
01:14:49.611 --> 01:14:52.656
This is a sign from Apollo.

666
01:14:52.948 --> 01:14:55.075
We will win a great victory tomorrow.

667
01:14:55.242 --> 01:14:56.785
Bird signs.

668
01:14:56.994 --> 01:14:59.830
You want to plan a strategy
based on bird signs.

669
01:14:59.997 --> 01:15:01.540
Hector. show respect.

670
01:15:02.332 --> 01:15:06.753
When Archeptolemus prophesied
four years of drought we dug deeper wells.

671
01:15:06.920 --> 01:15:10.007
The drought came
and we had water to drink.

672
01:15:10.174 --> 01:15:13.051
The high priest is a servant of the gods.

673
01:15:13.218 --> 01:15:15.220
And I am a servant of Troy.

674
01:15:17.014 --> 01:15:19.933
I've always honored the gods. Father.
You know that.

675
01:15:20.100 --> 01:15:23.645
But today I fought a Greek
who desecrated the statue of Apollo.

676
01:15:23.812 --> 01:15:26.523
Apollo didn't strike the man down.

677
01:15:27.608 --> 01:15:30.027
The gods won't fight this war for us.

678
01:15:31.278 --> 01:15:33.113
There won't be a war.

679
01:15:38.160 --> 01:15:40.120
This is not a conflict of nations.

680
01:15:40.329 --> 01:15:42.581
It is a dispute between two men.

681
01:15:43.665 --> 01:15:46.210
I don't want to see another Trojan die
because of me.

682
01:15:46.418 --> 01:15:48.128
Paris.

683
01:15:49.463 --> 01:15:52.966
Tomorrow morning. I will Challenge
Menelaus for the right to Helen.

684
01:15:53.133 --> 01:15:58.889
The winner will take her home.
The loser will burn before nightfall.

685
01:16:11.485 --> 01:16:12.819
Does he have a chance?

686
01:16:23.789 --> 01:16:25.332
Father...

687
01:16:26.541 --> 01:16:29.211
...I'm sorry for the pain I've caused you.

688
01:16:30.003 --> 01:16:31.964
Do you love her?

689
01:16:34.633 --> 01:16:38.845
You are a great king because you love
your country so much.

690
01:16:39.388 --> 01:16:41.223
Every blade of grass.

691
01:16:42.307 --> 01:16:44.184
Every grain of sand.

692
01:16:44.518 --> 01:16:45.936
Every rock in the river.

693
01:16:47.020 --> 01:16:49.273
You love all of Troy.

694
01:16:52.150 --> 01:16:54.027
That is the way I love Helen.

695
01:16:57.447 --> 01:17:00.534
I've fought many wars in my time.

696
01:17:01.868 --> 01:17:05.539
Some were fought for land.
some for power. some for glory.

697
01:17:07.416 --> 01:17:13.088
I suppose fighting for love makes
more sense than all the rest.

698
01:17:13.255 --> 01:17:16.174
But I won't be the one fighting.

699
01:17:19.553 --> 01:17:21.221
The sword of Troy.

700
01:17:21.930 --> 01:17:25.600
My father carried this sword.
and his father before him...

701
01:17:25.767 --> 01:17:28.395
...all the way back
to the founding of Troy.

702
01:17:28.562 --> 01:17:32.733
The history of our people
was written with this sword.

703
01:17:35.068 --> 01:17:37.237
Carry it with you tomorrow.

704
01:17:40.824 --> 01:17:44.161
The spirit of Troy is in that sword.

705
01:17:46.163 --> 01:17:49.291
So long as a Trojan carries it...

706
01:17:50.292 --> 01:17:52.919
...our people have a future.

707
01:17:57.049 --> 01:18:00.260
The man who killed Tecton
outside Apollo's temple...

708
01:18:01.261 --> 01:18:03.972
...I've never seen a spear
thrown like that.

709
01:18:05.140 --> 01:18:06.725
An impossible throw.

710
01:18:10.145 --> 01:18:12.439
He has no idea what's happening.

711
01:18:12.606 --> 01:18:13.648
Thank the gods.

712
01:18:15.317 --> 01:18:17.110
Don't go tomorrow.

713
01:18:18.111 --> 01:18:20.864
-Please don't go.
-Paris fights tomorrow. not me.

714
01:18:21.031 --> 01:18:26.453
Fifty thousand Greeks didn't cross the sea
to watch your brother fight. You know this.

715
01:18:28.789 --> 01:18:30.624
You'd make a fine general. my love.

716
01:18:30.791 --> 01:18:35.295
You've been fighting your whole life.
Let other men do battle this time.

717
01:18:35.629 --> 01:18:40.300
You know I don't want to fight.
I want to see my son grow tall.

718
01:18:40.467 --> 01:18:42.594
I want to see the girls chasing after him.

719
01:18:43.178 --> 01:18:44.930
Just like they chased his father.

720
01:18:46.973 --> 01:18:49.851
He's much more handsome than I ever was.

721
01:18:52.479 --> 01:18:53.980
I must see Paris.

722
01:18:54.147 --> 01:18:55.982
I lost...

723
01:18:56.691 --> 01:18:58.693
...seven brothers...

724
01:18:59.069 --> 01:19:01.446
...in the Spartan wars.

725
01:19:03.198 --> 01:19:05.992
You'd think I'd be good at losing by now.

726
01:19:08.870 --> 01:19:11.081
I can't lose you.

727
01:19:12.499 --> 01:19:14.292
I won't survive.

728
01:19:39.901 --> 01:19:41.445
Wait.

729
01:19:42.404 --> 01:19:43.864
Wait!

730
01:19:49.286 --> 01:19:50.704
Helen. what are you doing?

731
01:19:50.871 --> 01:19:52.998
-Let me go.
-No.

732
01:20:00.213 --> 01:20:02.382
I saw them burn.

733
01:20:03.717 --> 01:20:06.344
I saw them burning on the pyres.

734
01:20:08.597 --> 01:20:10.223
That's my fault.

735
01:20:11.266 --> 01:20:14.019
It is. You know it is.

736
01:20:15.937 --> 01:20:17.731
All those widows.

737
01:20:18.815 --> 01:20:21.109
I still hear them screaming.

738
01:20:22.777 --> 01:20:25.947
Their husbands died because I'm here.

739
01:20:26.823 --> 01:20:28.533
I'm going down to the ships.

740
01:20:28.700 --> 01:20:30.368
No. you're not.

741
01:20:30.577 --> 01:20:33.580
I'm giving myself back to Menelaus.

742
01:20:33.914 --> 01:20:35.790
He can do what he wants.

743
01:20:35.957 --> 01:20:38.126
Kill me. make me his slave. I don't care.

744
01:20:38.293 --> 01:20:39.753
Anything is better than this.

745
01:20:39.920 --> 01:20:41.546
It's too late for that.

746
01:20:41.713 --> 01:20:44.758
Do you think Agamemnon cares
about his brother's marriage?

747
01:20:44.925 --> 01:20:47.344
This is about power. Not love.

748
01:20:47.928 --> 01:20:50.347
Paris is going to fight in the morning.

749
01:20:51.389 --> 01:20:53.975
-Yes.
-Menelaus will kill him.

750
01:20:54.142 --> 01:20:55.477
I won't let that happen.

751
01:20:56.102 --> 01:20:58.104
-it's his decision.
-No.

752
01:20:58.438 --> 01:21:01.107
I can't ask anyone to fight for me.

753
01:21:02.567 --> 01:21:04.778
I'm no longer queen of Sparta.

754
01:21:07.155 --> 01:21:09.407
You're a princess of Troy now...

755
01:21:10.784 --> 01:21:13.328
...and my brother needs you tonight.

756
01:21:47.112 --> 01:21:48.780
My lord.

757
01:21:52.826 --> 01:21:54.828
The army is marching.

758
01:21:56.246 --> 01:21:58.164
Let them march. We stay.

759
01:21:59.332 --> 01:22:00.500
But the men are ready.

760
01:22:00.667 --> 01:22:03.503
We stay till Agamemnon groans
to have Achilles back.

761
01:22:05.171 --> 01:22:06.506
As you wish.

762
01:22:25.025 --> 01:22:26.568
Are you ready to fight?

763
01:22:27.777 --> 01:22:28.778
I am.

764
01:22:28.945 --> 01:22:31.364
Are you ready to kill? To take life?

765
01:22:41.333 --> 01:22:45.170
At night. I see their faces.
all the men I've killed.

766
01:22:46.296 --> 01:22:49.257
They're standing there on the far bank
of the River Styx.

767
01:22:52.344 --> 01:22:54.054
They're waiting for me.

768
01:22:56.181 --> 01:22:58.183
They say. "Welcome. brother."

769
01:23:05.398 --> 01:23:07.317
We men are wretched things.

770
01:23:12.614 --> 01:23:16.368
I taught you how to fight.
but I never taught you why to fight.

771
01:23:16.826 --> 01:23:18.078
I fight for you.

772
01:23:18.244 --> 01:23:20.246
Who will you fight for when I'm gone?

773
01:23:23.083 --> 01:23:26.294
Soldiers. they fight for kings
they've never even met.

774
01:23:27.295 --> 01:23:30.048
They do what they're told.
die when they're told to.

775
01:23:31.466 --> 01:23:32.842
Soldiers obey.

776
01:23:40.183 --> 01:23:43.436
Don't waste your life following
some fool's orders.

777
01:23:47.857 --> 01:23:49.275
Go.

778
01:25:14.277 --> 01:25:16.237
Are you sure you want to do this?

779
01:25:17.363 --> 01:25:19.073
I started this war.

780
01:25:34.714 --> 01:25:36.633
Helen...

781
01:25:37.801 --> 01:25:39.260
...sit with me.

782
01:25:48.520 --> 01:25:53.024
All my life I have prayed against this day.

783
01:25:54.400 --> 01:25:56.069
Yes. my king.

784
01:25:56.236 --> 01:25:59.239
Call me Father. dear child.

785
01:26:02.992 --> 01:26:05.245
Forgive me. Father...

786
01:26:06.496 --> 01:26:07.997
...for bringing this.

787
01:26:08.164 --> 01:26:11.042
I blame you for nothing.

788
01:26:11.376 --> 01:26:15.255
Everything is in the hands of the gods.

789
01:26:15.588 --> 01:26:17.173
Besides...

790
01:26:17.340 --> 01:26:21.928
...how could I blame anyone
for falling in love with Paris?

791
01:28:33.935 --> 01:28:37.647
Prepare to halt!

792
01:28:37.981 --> 01:28:39.565
Halt!

793
01:28:58.918 --> 01:29:00.586
Move.

794
01:29:10.930 --> 01:29:12.432
Menelaus is a bull.

795
01:29:12.598 --> 01:29:17.020
He'll charge you.
but keep your distance and use your speed.

796
01:29:18.438 --> 01:29:19.731
Brother...

797
01:29:20.523 --> 01:29:22.692
...you don't have to do this.

798
01:29:44.088 --> 01:29:48.426
I see you're not hiding behind
your high walls. Valiant of you.

799
01:29:48.593 --> 01:29:51.345
III-advised. but valiant.

800
01:29:51.512 --> 01:29:55.266
You come here uninvited.
Go back to your ships and go home.

801
01:29:55.433 --> 01:29:57.435
We've come too far. Prince Hector.

802
01:29:57.602 --> 01:30:00.063
Prince? What prince?

803
01:30:00.229 --> 01:30:03.066
What son of a king would accept
a man's hospitality...

804
01:30:03.232 --> 01:30:07.570
...eat his food. drink his wine. then steal
his wife in the middle of the night?

805
01:30:07.737 --> 01:30:09.822
The sun was shining
when your wife left you.

806
01:30:11.866 --> 01:30:14.744
She's up there. watching.
isn't she? Good.

807
01:30:14.911 --> 01:30:17.163
I want her to watch you die.

808
01:30:18.164 --> 01:30:19.499
Not yet. brother.

809
01:30:21.584 --> 01:30:23.377
Look around you. Hector.

810
01:30:23.544 --> 01:30:27.131
I brought all the warriors of Greece
to your shores.

811
01:30:27.298 --> 01:30:29.300
You can still save Troy. young prince.

812
01:30:29.467 --> 01:30:30.927
I have two wishes.

813
01:30:31.094 --> 01:30:34.430
If you grant them.
no more of your people need die.

814
01:30:34.639 --> 01:30:37.600
First. you must give Helen
back to my brother.

815
01:30:38.017 --> 01:30:41.354
Second. Troy must submit
to my command...

816
01:30:41.604 --> 01:30:44.232
...to fight for me whenever I call.

817
01:30:44.398 --> 01:30:47.443
You want me to look upon your army
and tremble?

818
01:30:49.737 --> 01:30:51.239
Well. I see them.

819
01:30:51.739 --> 01:30:56.452
I see 50.000 men brought here
to fight for one man's greed.

820
01:31:00.206 --> 01:31:01.707
Careful. boy.

821
01:31:03.000 --> 01:31:04.794
My mercy has limits.

822
01:31:04.961 --> 01:31:07.380
And I've seen the limits of your mercy.

823
01:31:07.547 --> 01:31:12.009
And I tell you now. no son of Troy
will ever submit to a foreign ruler.

824
01:31:12.260 --> 01:31:16.389
Then every son of Troy shall die.

825
01:31:19.684 --> 01:31:21.561
There is another way.

826
01:31:23.729 --> 01:31:27.942
I love Helen. I won't give her up
and neither will you.

827
01:31:28.109 --> 01:31:29.777
So let us fight our own battle.

828
01:31:30.027 --> 01:31:33.739
The winner takes Helen home.
And let that be the end of it.

829
01:31:33.906 --> 01:31:37.577
A brave offer. but not enough.

830
01:31:39.078 --> 01:31:40.830
Let me kill this little peacock.

831
01:31:40.997 --> 01:31:45.751
I didn't come here for your pretty wife.
I came here for Troy.

832
01:31:45.918 --> 01:31:48.212
I came for my honor.

833
01:31:48.379 --> 01:31:50.798
His every breath insults me.

834
01:31:51.382 --> 01:31:54.760
Let me kill him. When he's lying
in the dust. signal to attack.

835
01:31:54.927 --> 01:31:58.097
You'll have your city.
I'll have my revenge.

836
01:32:03.686 --> 01:32:05.104
So be it.

837
01:32:09.442 --> 01:32:13.738
I accept your challenge. And tonight.
I'll drink to your bones.

838
01:32:23.372 --> 01:32:26.459
-My lord.
-Back to the line!

839
01:32:41.140 --> 01:32:43.434
Make him swing and miss. He'll tire.

840
01:32:45.144 --> 01:32:46.479
Brother...

841
01:32:46.646 --> 01:32:49.732
...if I fall. tell Helen-- Tell her--

842
01:32:49.899 --> 01:32:51.651
I will.

843
01:32:51.817 --> 01:32:53.903
Don't let Menelaus hurt her. If he--

844
01:32:54.070 --> 01:32:57.490
You think of your sword and his sword
and nothing else.

845
01:34:09.145 --> 01:34:10.771
Get up.

846
01:34:11.188 --> 01:34:12.898
Come on.

847
01:34:58.194 --> 01:34:59.612
See the crows?

848
01:35:01.614 --> 01:35:03.741
They never tasted prince before.

849
01:35:38.109 --> 01:35:42.488
Is this what you left me for?!

850
01:35:42.655 --> 01:35:44.323
Fight!

851
01:35:44.657 --> 01:35:45.991
Fight me!

852
01:35:47.159 --> 01:35:48.369
You coward!

853
01:35:48.536 --> 01:35:49.829
Fight me!

854
01:35:49.995 --> 01:35:52.373
We have a pact! Fight!

855
01:35:52.915 --> 01:35:55.876
Fight him. son. Fight him.

856
01:35:56.043 --> 01:35:59.839
-Fight me!
-The Trojans have violated the agreement!

857
01:36:00.005 --> 01:36:02.550
Prepare for battle!

858
01:36:04.301 --> 01:36:05.636
This is not honor!

859
01:36:05.886 --> 01:36:08.347
This is not worthy of royalty!

860
01:36:08.764 --> 01:36:11.892
If he doesn't fight. Troy is doomed.

861
01:36:12.810 --> 01:36:14.019
Paris.

862
01:36:15.521 --> 01:36:17.481
No. No.

863
01:36:18.232 --> 01:36:19.525
The fight is over.

864
01:36:19.692 --> 01:36:21.861
The fight is not over.

865
01:36:22.027 --> 01:36:23.737
Stand back. Prince Hector.

866
01:36:23.904 --> 01:36:26.574
I'll kill him at your feet. I don't care.

867
01:36:26.740 --> 01:36:28.033
He is my brother.

868
01:37:23.631 --> 01:37:25.382
Paris!

869
01:37:34.475 --> 01:37:36.185
Go! Go!

870
01:37:43.025 --> 01:37:44.860
Get inside. Paris!

871
01:37:45.444 --> 01:37:46.737
Archers!

872
01:37:50.157 --> 01:37:53.369
-Our men are too close to the walls.
-Pull back.

873
01:37:53.536 --> 01:37:55.246
Pull back. you fool!

874
01:37:55.496 --> 01:37:58.040
For Troy!

875
01:38:24.567 --> 01:38:26.735
-Now!
-Loose!

876
01:38:58.350 --> 01:38:59.768
Get them in line!

877
01:39:06.191 --> 01:39:09.153
Get the men back into lines!

878
01:39:09.320 --> 01:39:11.697
Front line. push!

879
01:40:21.058 --> 01:40:23.894
So you're the best of the Trojans.

880
01:41:39.261 --> 01:41:40.763
Forward.

881
01:41:40.929 --> 01:41:42.181
Forward!

882
01:41:58.614 --> 01:41:59.907
Forward!

883
01:42:14.838 --> 01:42:17.216
Apollonians! Now!

884
01:42:31.188 --> 01:42:32.523
Prince Hector!

885
01:42:40.697 --> 01:42:42.032
We need to retreat!

886
01:42:42.991 --> 01:42:45.202
My army's never lost a battle yet!

887
01:42:45.369 --> 01:42:47.871
You won't have an army
if you don't fall back!

888
01:42:56.255 --> 01:42:58.298
Back to the ships!

889
01:42:58.465 --> 01:43:00.175
-Back to the ships!
-Retreat!

890
01:43:00.342 --> 01:43:01.343
-Back!
-Retreat!

891
01:43:01.510 --> 01:43:03.303
Go back!

892
01:43:11.478 --> 01:43:13.313
Back. Back to the ships!

893
01:44:19.922 --> 01:44:21.506
Fall back!

894
01:44:21.882 --> 01:44:24.384
-Men. fall back!
-Halt!

895
01:44:31.642 --> 01:44:33.060
Halt!

896
01:44:33.268 --> 01:44:34.728
But we have them on the run!

897
01:44:34.978 --> 01:44:37.189
We're in range of their archers.

898
01:44:37.356 --> 01:44:39.232
Have our men gather our fallen.

899
01:44:39.399 --> 01:44:42.361
Send an emissary to them.
They can collect their dead.

900
01:44:42.527 --> 01:44:45.030
Would they have done the same for us?

901
01:44:47.991 --> 01:44:49.576
Go! Back!

902
01:44:50.452 --> 01:44:52.162
Fall back into line!

903
01:45:56.852 --> 01:45:59.062
Before I leave...

904
01:45:59.312 --> 01:46:02.858
...I will burn their city to the ground.

905
01:46:03.025 --> 01:46:06.862
Brother. I promise you that.

906
01:46:35.348 --> 01:46:40.604
They're laughing at me in Troy.
Drunk with victory!

907
01:46:40.979 --> 01:46:43.982
They think I'll sail home at first light.

908
01:46:44.149 --> 01:46:45.484
Maybe we should.

909
01:46:45.650 --> 01:46:47.986
Flee? Like a whipped dog?

910
01:46:48.195 --> 01:46:51.823
The men believe we came here
for Menelaus' wife.

911
01:46:53.075 --> 01:46:54.743
Won't be needing her anymore.

912
01:46:54.951 --> 01:46:58.080
My brother's blood still wets the sand.
and you insult him!

913
01:46:58.288 --> 01:47:00.916
It's no insult to say a dead man is dead.

914
01:47:01.124 --> 01:47:04.211
If we leave now. we lose all credibility.

915
01:47:04.419 --> 01:47:08.840
The Trojans can beat us so easily.
How long before the Hittites invade?

916
01:47:09.007 --> 01:47:13.512
If we stay. we stay here
for the right reasons.

917
01:47:13.678 --> 01:47:15.847
To protect Greece. not your pride.

918
01:47:16.014 --> 01:47:18.767
Your private battle with Achilles
is destroying us.

919
01:47:18.934 --> 01:47:20.185
Achilles is one man.

920
01:47:20.352 --> 01:47:22.771
Hector is one man.

921
01:47:23.355 --> 01:47:24.773
Look what he did to us today.

922
01:47:24.981 --> 01:47:28.944
Hector fights for his country!
Achilles fights only for himself!

923
01:47:29.111 --> 01:47:33.865
I don't care about the man's allegiance.
I care about his ability to win battles.

924
01:47:34.116 --> 01:47:35.659
He's right.

925
01:47:35.826 --> 01:47:37.285
The men's morale is weak.

926
01:47:37.452 --> 01:47:40.580
Weak? They're ready to swim home.

927
01:47:40.747 --> 01:47:45.669
Even if I could make peace with Achilles.
the man won't listen to me!

928
01:47:46.545 --> 01:47:50.006
He's as likely to spear me
as to speak to me!

929
01:47:51.550 --> 01:47:53.009
I'll talk to him.

930
01:47:53.593 --> 01:47:55.011
He'll want the girl back.

931
01:47:55.554 --> 01:47:56.888
He can have that damn girl.

932
01:48:00.725 --> 01:48:01.935
I haven't touched her.

933
01:48:02.894 --> 01:48:04.187
Where is she?

934
01:48:05.730 --> 01:48:07.399
I gave her to the men.

935
01:48:09.401 --> 01:48:14.072
They need some amusement after today.

936
01:48:17.909 --> 01:48:20.203
Come on. give the bitch to me!

937
01:48:20.829 --> 01:48:22.205
Who's first?

938
01:48:22.956 --> 01:48:24.499
Trojan whore!

939
01:48:24.666 --> 01:48:26.585
What's this? A virgin's robe?

940
01:48:26.918 --> 01:48:29.921
-You won't be needing that for much longer!
-Hold her.

941
01:48:34.926 --> 01:48:37.804
Come on. Come on. Hold her down.

942
01:49:11.213 --> 01:49:13.048
Are you hurt?

943
01:49:19.179 --> 01:49:21.473
I watched you fight them.
You have courage.

944
01:49:21.640 --> 01:49:26.144
To fight back when people attack me?
Dog has that kind of courage.

945
01:49:49.501 --> 01:49:51.002
Eat.

946
01:49:59.636 --> 01:50:01.680
I've known men like you my whole life.

947
01:50:03.390 --> 01:50:04.516
No. you haven't.

948
01:50:04.683 --> 01:50:07.018
You think you're so different
from 1000 others?

949
01:50:07.894 --> 01:50:11.773
Soldiers understand nothing but war.
Peace confuses them.

950
01:50:12.023 --> 01:50:14.359
-And you hate these soldiers.
-I pity them.

951
01:50:15.318 --> 01:50:18.029
Trojan soldiers died trying to protect you.

952
01:50:18.530 --> 01:50:21.241
Perhaps they deserve more than your pity.

953
01:50:24.202 --> 01:50:25.829
Why did you choose this life?

954
01:50:26.246 --> 01:50:28.540
-What life?
-To be a great warrior.

955
01:50:31.042 --> 01:50:34.796
I chose nothing. I was born.
and this is what I am.

956
01:50:36.339 --> 01:50:39.426
And you? Why did you choose
to love a god?

957
01:50:40.385 --> 01:50:43.388
I think you'll find the romance one-sided.

958
01:50:45.974 --> 01:50:47.559
Do you enjoy provoking me?

959
01:50:49.519 --> 01:50:51.563
You've dedicated your life to the gods.

960
01:50:51.730 --> 01:50:55.400
Zeus. god of thunder. Athena.
goddess of wisdom. You serve them.

961
01:50:55.567 --> 01:50:58.069
-Yes. of course.
-And Ares. god of war?

962
01:50:58.236 --> 01:51:01.239
Who blankets his bed with the skin
of men he's killed?

963
01:51:02.991 --> 01:51:05.827
All the gods are to be feared
and respected.

964
01:51:17.088 --> 01:51:18.673
I'll tell you a secret...

965
01:51:19.257 --> 01:51:21.926
...something they don't teach you
in your temple.

966
01:51:32.437 --> 01:51:34.814
The gods envy us.

967
01:51:36.524 --> 01:51:38.610
They envy us because we're mortal.

968
01:51:40.153 --> 01:51:42.989
Because any moment might be our last.

969
01:51:43.281 --> 01:51:46.576
Everything's more beautiful
because we're doomed.

970
01:51:47.786 --> 01:51:50.747
You will never be lovelier
than you are now.

971
01:51:55.043 --> 01:51:56.795
We will never be here again.

972
01:52:07.555 --> 01:52:09.557
I thought you were a dumb brute.

973
01:52:13.144 --> 01:52:15.146
I could have forgiven a dumb brute.

974
01:52:39.504 --> 01:52:40.713
Do it.

975
01:52:47.262 --> 01:52:48.805
Nothing is easier.

976
01:52:48.972 --> 01:52:50.181
Aren't you afraid?

977
01:52:52.475 --> 01:52:57.063
Everyone dies. Today or 50 years
from now. What does it matter?

978
01:53:01.860 --> 01:53:03.653
Do it.

979
01:53:05.238 --> 01:53:07.407
You'll kill more men if I don't kill you.

980
01:53:07.574 --> 01:53:09.200
Many.

981
01:54:44.128 --> 01:54:45.630
My lord. there's--

982
01:55:00.478 --> 01:55:04.232
Tell the men to start loading the ship.
We're going home.

983
01:55:08.194 --> 01:55:09.988
Gather the stores.

984
01:55:10.154 --> 01:55:11.990
Prepare the ship.

985
01:55:12.991 --> 01:55:14.659
Prepare the ship.

986
01:55:14.951 --> 01:55:17.370
Agamemnon is a proud man.

987
01:55:18.454 --> 01:55:20.832
But he knows when he's made a mistake.

988
01:55:20.999 --> 01:55:23.251
The man sends you
to make his apologies?

989
01:55:25.378 --> 01:55:28.131
What are you doing enthralled
to that pig of a king?

990
01:55:29.132 --> 01:55:31.384
The world seems simple to you.
my friend...

991
01:55:31.551 --> 01:55:35.054
...but when you're a king.
very few choices are simple.

992
01:55:37.056 --> 01:55:39.892
Ithaca cannot afford an enemy
like Agamemnon.

993
01:55:40.059 --> 01:55:41.728
Are we supposed to fear him?

994
01:55:41.894 --> 01:55:46.774
You don't fear anyone.
That's your problem. Fear is useful.

995
01:55:49.986 --> 01:55:51.446
We need you back.

996
01:55:51.696 --> 01:55:53.448
Greece needs you.

997
01:55:54.365 --> 01:55:57.118
Greece got along fine before I was born.

998
01:55:57.285 --> 01:55:59.537
Greece will be Greece long after I'm dead.

999
01:55:59.704 --> 01:56:01.748
I'm not talking about the land.

1000
01:56:01.914 --> 01:56:04.167
The men need you.

1001
01:56:07.629 --> 01:56:09.213
Stay. Achilles.

1002
01:56:10.214 --> 01:56:11.758
You were born for this war.

1003
01:56:15.678 --> 01:56:17.263
Things are less simple today.

1004
01:56:19.265 --> 01:56:23.561
Women have a way
of complicating things.

1005
01:56:27.273 --> 01:56:30.568
Of all the kings of Greece.
I respect you the most.

1006
01:56:30.860 --> 01:56:32.904
But in this war. you're a servant.

1007
01:56:33.071 --> 01:56:36.240
Sometimes you have to serve
in order to lead.

1008
01:56:37.867 --> 01:56:40.745
I hope you understand that one day.

1009
01:56:45.958 --> 01:56:47.210
We're going home?

1010
01:56:51.756 --> 01:56:53.007
We sail in the morning.

1011
01:56:53.299 --> 01:56:56.761
Greeks are being slaughtered.
We can't just sail away.

1012
01:56:56.928 --> 01:57:00.765
If it's fighting you still long for.
there will always be another war.

1013
01:57:00.932 --> 01:57:02.350
These are our countrymen.

1014
01:57:02.934 --> 01:57:06.104
I ate. laughed. mourned with these men
while you hid in your tent.

1015
01:57:07.188 --> 01:57:10.191
You betray all of Greece
just to see Agamemnon fall.

1016
01:57:14.404 --> 01:57:16.239
Someone has to lose.

1017
01:57:17.323 --> 01:57:21.411
In all my years to come.
may my heart never turn as black as yours!

1018
01:57:21.703 --> 01:57:23.955
We sail in the morning!

1019
01:57:29.877 --> 01:57:32.296
The omens are gathering.

1020
01:57:32.463 --> 01:57:34.298
The directive is clear.

1021
01:57:34.465 --> 01:57:36.718
Fight for your country.
that's the only directive.

1022
01:57:36.884 --> 01:57:41.806
Last time the high priest spoke to us.
he prophesied a great victory for Troy.

1023
01:57:41.973 --> 01:57:45.727
We won a great victory. Let him speak.

1024
01:57:46.352 --> 01:57:48.813
What course of action
do you recommend?

1025
01:57:49.105 --> 01:57:51.482
The gods favor our cause.

1026
01:57:51.649 --> 01:57:54.861
Now is the time to destroy
the Greek army.

1027
01:57:56.487 --> 01:57:57.780
Glaucus?

1028
01:57:58.656 --> 01:58:00.950
Their morale is battered.

1029
01:58:01.117 --> 01:58:04.328
Hit them now. Hit them hard.

1030
01:58:04.495 --> 01:58:06.330
And they will run.

1031
01:58:09.167 --> 01:58:12.795
I must admit.
I overestimated the Greeks.

1032
01:58:13.504 --> 01:58:16.215
They lack discipline and courage.

1033
01:58:23.347 --> 01:58:27.643
The Myrmidons didn't fight yesterday. There
must be dissension among the Greeks.

1034
01:58:27.810 --> 01:58:30.438
But if we attack their ships.
we will unify them.

1035
01:58:31.189 --> 01:58:33.191
If they decide to attack us. let them.

1036
01:58:33.357 --> 01:58:36.277
Our walls can't be breached.
We'll beat them back again.

1037
01:58:40.406 --> 01:58:42.909
Yesterday. the Greeks underestimated us.

1038
01:58:43.868 --> 01:58:46.037
We should not return the favor.

1039
01:58:59.801 --> 01:59:02.512
You're confident about the meaning
of these omens?

1040
01:59:02.678 --> 01:59:06.349
The desecration of his temple
angers Apollo.

1041
01:59:06.849 --> 01:59:09.811
The gods have cursed the Greeks.

1042
01:59:10.311 --> 01:59:14.106
Two of their kings
have already gone down to the dust.

1043
01:59:19.237 --> 01:59:22.073
Prepare the army. We attack at daybreak.

1044
01:59:22.240 --> 01:59:23.741
Father.

1045
01:59:24.742 --> 01:59:26.702
We're making a mistake.

1046
01:59:29.205 --> 01:59:30.498
Prepare the army.

1047
01:59:48.558 --> 01:59:50.142
Come on.

1048
02:00:17.795 --> 02:00:19.922
Am I still your captive?

1049
02:00:22.800 --> 02:00:24.343
You're my guest.

1050
02:00:26.971 --> 02:00:30.099
In Troy. guests can leave
whenever they want.

1051
02:00:30.266 --> 02:00:31.934
You should leave. then.

1052
02:00:38.858 --> 02:00:40.902
Would you leave this all behind?

1053
02:00:45.323 --> 02:00:46.991
Would you leave Troy?

1054
02:03:47.505 --> 02:03:49.340
Hold those barricades!

1055
02:04:10.194 --> 02:04:12.154
Archers to the rear.

1056
02:04:21.539 --> 02:04:23.707
Achilles.

1057
02:04:46.856 --> 02:04:48.691
Achilles.

1058
02:04:51.569 --> 02:04:53.195
Now!

1059
02:05:02.329 --> 02:05:03.747
Forward!

1060
02:07:58.130 --> 02:07:59.757
Enough for one day.

1061
02:08:01.925 --> 02:08:03.177
Yes.

1062
02:08:04.678 --> 02:08:08.766
Back to the ships!

1063
02:08:10.601 --> 02:08:12.311
It was his cousin.

1064
02:08:16.690 --> 02:08:18.275
To Troy!

1065
02:08:19.193 --> 02:08:21.362
Back to the City!

1066
02:08:22.279 --> 02:08:23.655
To Troy!

1067
02:08:25.783 --> 02:08:27.951
We were going to sail home today.

1068
02:08:30.788 --> 02:08:33.457
I don't think anyone's sailing home now.

1069
02:08:54.186 --> 02:08:55.646
Achilles.

1070
02:09:11.161 --> 02:09:12.996
You violated my command.

1071
02:09:13.789 --> 02:09:17.084
No. my lord. There was a mistake.

1072
02:09:18.001 --> 02:09:20.546
I ordered the Myrmidons to stand down.

1073
02:09:20.838 --> 02:09:22.965
You led them into combat.

1074
02:09:27.845 --> 02:09:31.723
I didn't lead them. my lord.
We thought you did.

1075
02:09:39.481 --> 02:09:40.732
Where's Patroclus?

1076
02:09:43.694 --> 02:09:45.404
Patroclus!

1077
02:09:45.863 --> 02:09:48.157
We thought he was you. my lord.

1078
02:09:50.617 --> 02:09:56.373
He wore your armor. your shield.
your greaves. your helmet.

1079
02:09:57.291 --> 02:09:59.084
He even moved like you.

1080
02:09:59.877 --> 02:10:01.962
Where is he?

1081
02:10:05.757 --> 02:10:07.634
-Where?
-He's dead. my lord.

1082
02:10:08.719 --> 02:10:10.220
Hector out his throat.

1083
02:10:21.064 --> 02:10:23.484
Don't. Don't.

1084
02:10:56.266 --> 02:10:58.018
Where are you taking me?

1085
02:11:03.815 --> 02:11:05.776
Do you remember how to get here?

1086
02:11:06.360 --> 02:11:07.986
Yes.

1087
02:11:15.536 --> 02:11:18.580
The next time you come here.
follow the tunnel.

1088
02:11:18.747 --> 02:11:21.833
There are no turns. so you can't get lost.
Just keep walking.

1089
02:11:22.000 --> 02:11:23.418
Why?

1090
02:11:23.919 --> 02:11:26.421
When you get to the end.
you'll be by the river.

1091
02:11:26.588 --> 02:11:29.007
Follow the river until you get
to Mount Ida.

1092
02:11:29.841 --> 02:11:32.219
The Greeks won't go that far inland.

1093
02:11:33.011 --> 02:11:34.638
Hector.

1094
02:11:35.347 --> 02:11:37.015
Why are you telling me this?

1095
02:11:42.604 --> 02:11:44.064
-If I die--
-No.

1096
02:11:44.231 --> 02:11:47.484
If I die. I don't know how long
the city will stand.

1097
02:11:47.901 --> 02:11:49.069
Don't say that.

1098
02:11:49.236 --> 02:11:51.488
If the Greeks get inside the walls.
it's over.

1099
02:11:52.197 --> 02:11:55.617
They'll kill all the men. throw
the babies from the city walls.

1100
02:11:55.784 --> 02:11:58.161
-Please.
-The women. they'll take as slaves.

1101
02:11:58.328 --> 02:12:00.998
That. for you. will be worse than dying.

1102
02:12:01.248 --> 02:12:03.959
Why are you saying such things?

1103
02:12:06.837 --> 02:12:08.797
Because I want you to be ready.

1104
02:12:11.174 --> 02:12:15.012
I want you to get our boy.
and I want you to bring him here.

1105
02:12:16.346 --> 02:12:20.851
You save as many people as you can.
but you get here. And you run.

1106
02:12:22.519 --> 02:12:23.729
Do you understand?

1107
02:12:31.069 --> 02:12:32.821
I killed a boy today.

1108
02:12:34.740 --> 02:12:36.408
And he was young.

1109
02:12:37.576 --> 02:12:39.411
He was much too young.

1110
02:13:14.571 --> 02:13:17.407
That boy has just saved this war for us.

1111
02:15:05.056 --> 02:15:07.225
-Eudorus.
-My lord.

1112
02:15:07.392 --> 02:15:09.186
I need my armor.

1113
02:16:10.080 --> 02:16:11.414
No.

1114
02:16:12.958 --> 02:16:14.292
Don't go!

1115
02:16:15.168 --> 02:16:17.087
Rope!

1116
02:16:17.254 --> 02:16:19.589
Hector's my cousin. He's a good man.

1117
02:16:20.173 --> 02:16:22.968
Don't fight him. Please don't fight him.

1118
02:16:23.385 --> 02:16:25.303
Please.

1119
02:17:41.838 --> 02:17:43.173
No.

1120
02:18:09.074 --> 02:18:11.076
Hector!

1121
02:18:17.290 --> 02:18:19.000
Hector!

1122
02:18:26.925 --> 02:18:28.885
Hector!

1123
02:18:33.890 --> 02:18:35.392
Hector!

1124
02:18:39.312 --> 02:18:41.272
Father...

1125
02:18:41.439 --> 02:18:43.817
...forgive me for any offenses.

1126
02:18:45.694 --> 02:18:47.946
I've served you as best as I could.

1127
02:18:48.530 --> 02:18:50.198
Hector!

1128
02:18:54.452 --> 02:18:56.871
May the gods be with you.

1129
02:19:01.251 --> 02:19:02.460
Hector.

1130
02:19:05.255 --> 02:19:08.591
No father ever had a better son.

1131
02:19:15.265 --> 02:19:16.850
Hector!

1132
02:19:18.727 --> 02:19:20.353
Apollo guard you. my prince.

1133
02:19:27.610 --> 02:19:29.029
You're the best man I know.

1134
02:19:35.285 --> 02:19:37.120
You're a prince of Troy.

1135
02:19:37.912 --> 02:19:39.456
I know you'll make me proud.

1136
02:19:47.255 --> 02:19:49.924
Hector!

1137
02:20:06.941 --> 02:20:09.027
Remember what I told you.

1138
02:20:09.819 --> 02:20:12.822
You don't have to go. You don't.

1139
02:20:13.114 --> 02:20:14.908
You remember what I told you.

1140
02:20:33.259 --> 02:20:35.678
Hector!

1141
02:20:51.194 --> 02:20:53.780
Hector!

1142
02:22:07.770 --> 02:22:10.440
I've seen this moment in my dreams.

1143
02:22:12.609 --> 02:22:13.985
I'll make a pact with you.

1144
02:22:14.944 --> 02:22:16.988
With the gods as our witnesses...

1145
02:22:17.155 --> 02:22:21.868
...let us pledge that the winner will allow
the loser all the proper funeral rituals.

1146
02:22:22.035 --> 02:22:25.038
There are no pacts
between lions and men.

1147
02:22:33.046 --> 02:22:35.340
Now you know who you're fighting.

1148
02:22:43.848 --> 02:22:46.684
I thought it was you
I was fighting yesterday.

1149
02:22:47.018 --> 02:22:51.022
And I wish it had been you. But I gave
the dead boy the honor he deserved.

1150
02:22:51.189 --> 02:22:53.191
You gave him the honor of your sword.

1151
02:22:54.150 --> 02:22:57.070
You won't have eyes tonight.
You won't have ears or a tongue.

1152
02:22:57.237 --> 02:23:01.449
You'll wander the underworld. blind. deaf.
and dumb. and all the dead will know:

1153
02:23:01.616 --> 02:23:05.328
This is Hector. the fool who thought
he killed Achilles.

1154
02:25:03.404 --> 02:25:04.697
Get up. prince of Troy.

1155
02:25:07.325 --> 02:25:10.286
Get up. I won't let a stone take my glory.

1156
02:28:43.124 --> 02:28:45.001
You lost your cousin.

1157
02:28:46.836 --> 02:28:48.671
Now you've taken mine.

1158
02:28:52.133 --> 02:28:53.718
When does it end?

1159
02:28:55.761 --> 02:28:57.305
It never ends.

1160
02:29:57.239 --> 02:29:58.783
Who are you?

1161
02:29:58.949 --> 02:30:04.830
I have endured what no one
on earth has endured before.

1162
02:30:05.498 --> 02:30:10.795
I kissed the hands of the man
who killed my son.

1163
02:30:17.927 --> 02:30:19.595
Priam?

1164
02:30:21.138 --> 02:30:22.515
How did you get in here?

1165
02:30:22.682 --> 02:30:26.644
I know my own Country better
than the Greeks. I think.

1166
02:30:31.399 --> 02:30:33.818
You're a brave man.

1167
02:30:36.612 --> 02:30:39.782
I could have your head on a spit
in the blink of an eye.

1168
02:30:40.157 --> 02:30:43.953
Do you really think death
frightens me now?

1169
02:30:45.705 --> 02:30:48.290
I watched my eldest son die...

1170
02:30:48.457 --> 02:30:52.336
...watched you drag his body
behind your chariot.

1171
02:30:55.548 --> 02:30:57.717
Give him back to me.

1172
02:30:58.801 --> 02:31:03.305
He deserves the honor of a proper burial.
You know that.

1173
02:31:04.265 --> 02:31:06.475
Give him to me.

1174
02:31:07.393 --> 02:31:09.103
He killed my cousin.

1175
02:31:09.270 --> 02:31:11.230
He thought it was you.

1176
02:31:13.816 --> 02:31:16.527
How many cousins have you killed?

1177
02:31:18.070 --> 02:31:21.991
How many sons and fathers
and brothers and husbands?

1178
02:31:22.199 --> 02:31:24.785
How many. brave Achilles?

1179
02:31:29.665 --> 02:31:31.792
I knew your father.

1180
02:31:32.918 --> 02:31:35.212
He died before his time.

1181
02:31:36.505 --> 02:31:41.677
But he was lucky not to live long enough
to see his son fall.

1182
02:31:46.599 --> 02:31:49.268
You have taken everything from me.

1183
02:31:51.353 --> 02:31:53.189
My eldest son...

1184
02:31:53.814 --> 02:31:55.608
...heir to my throne...

1185
02:31:56.025 --> 02:31:58.652
...defender of my kingdom.

1186
02:32:00.029 --> 02:32:04.700
I cannot change what happened.
It is the will of the gods.

1187
02:32:05.993 --> 02:32:09.330
But give me this small mercy.

1188
02:32:11.665 --> 02:32:15.795
I loved my boy from the moment
he opened his eyes...

1189
02:32:15.961 --> 02:32:18.798
...till the moment you closed them.

1190
02:32:21.217 --> 02:32:24.220
Let me wash his body.

1191
02:32:25.846 --> 02:32:29.058
Let me say the prayers.

1192
02:32:30.351 --> 02:32:35.397
Let me place two coins on his eyes
for the boatman.

1193
02:32:40.110 --> 02:32:42.363
If I let you walk out of here...

1194
02:32:44.657 --> 02:32:46.575
...if I let you take him...

1195
02:32:49.245 --> 02:32:51.288
...it doesn't change anything.

1196
02:32:52.873 --> 02:32:55.543
You're still my enemy in the morning.

1197
02:32:56.669 --> 02:32:59.713
You're still my enemy tonight.

1198
02:33:00.756 --> 02:33:04.343
But even enemies can show respect.

1199
02:33:24.029 --> 02:33:25.447
I admire your courage.

1200
02:33:33.163 --> 02:33:34.957
Meet me outside in a moment.

1201
02:34:21.003 --> 02:34:22.713
We'll meet again soon. my brother.

1202
02:34:57.373 --> 02:34:59.792
Your son was the best I've fought.

1203
02:35:03.045 --> 02:35:05.714
In my country. the funeral games
last for 12 days.

1204
02:35:06.215 --> 02:35:08.342
It is the same in my country.

1205
02:35:09.093 --> 02:35:11.261
Then the prince will have that honor.

1206
02:35:12.137 --> 02:35:15.432
No Greek will attack Troy for 12 days.

1207
02:35:21.563 --> 02:35:22.898
Briseis?

1208
02:35:26.026 --> 02:35:28.404
I thought you were dead.

1209
02:35:39.081 --> 02:35:40.374
You are free.

1210
02:35:56.807 --> 02:35:58.517
If I hurt you...

1211
02:36:00.894 --> 02:36:03.105
...it's not what I wanted.

1212
02:36:17.619 --> 02:36:18.912
Go.

1213
02:36:19.329 --> 02:36:22.499
No one will stop you. You have my word.

1214
02:36:23.292 --> 02:36:24.960
Come. my girl.

1215
02:36:32.134 --> 02:36:35.846
You're a far better king than the one
leading this army.

1216
02:36:52.362 --> 02:36:56.325
Achilles makes a secret pact. and I
have to honor it? What treason is this?

1217
02:36:56.742 --> 02:37:00.746
Consorting with the enemy king.
Giving him 12 days of peace.

1218
02:37:00.913 --> 02:37:03.040
Peace! Peace!

1219
02:37:03.332 --> 02:37:06.043
Their prince is dead.
Their army is leaderless.

1220
02:37:06.210 --> 02:37:07.836
This is the time to attack!

1221
02:37:08.170 --> 02:37:12.341
Even with Hector gone. we have
no way to breach their walls.

1222
02:37:12.925 --> 02:37:15.344
They can wait 10 years for us to leave.

1223
02:37:16.595 --> 02:37:19.306
I will smash their walls to the ground...

1224
02:37:19.473 --> 02:37:22.059
...if it costs me 40.000 Greeks.

1225
02:37:22.226 --> 02:37:24.853
Hear me. Zeus!

1226
02:37:25.020 --> 02:37:28.732
I will smash their walls to the ground.

1227
02:39:16.048 --> 02:39:17.466
That's good.

1228
02:39:17.841 --> 02:39:19.760
For my son back home.

1229
02:39:46.620 --> 02:39:48.163
Well. Odysseus.

1230
02:39:49.164 --> 02:39:53.835
You found a way to make the sheep
invite the wolves to dinner.

1231
02:40:12.229 --> 02:40:15.941
Forgive me. Eudorus.
I should never have struck you.

1232
02:40:18.235 --> 02:40:21.363
You've been a loyal friend all your life.

1233
02:40:24.533 --> 02:40:27.202
I hope I never disappoint you again.

1234
02:40:27.536 --> 02:40:30.038
It's I who have been the disappointment.

1235
02:40:33.542 --> 02:40:36.211
Rouse the men. You're taking them home.

1236
02:40:38.547 --> 02:40:40.382
Aren't you coming with us?

1237
02:40:41.174 --> 02:40:43.385
I have my own battle to fight.

1238
02:40:43.885 --> 02:40:45.554
Let me march beside you.

1239
02:40:45.721 --> 02:40:49.558
No. I don't want our men
to be a part of this.

1240
02:40:55.647 --> 02:40:57.482
It's a beautiful night.

1241
02:40:58.150 --> 02:41:01.445
Go. Eudorus.
This is the last order I give you.

1242
02:41:07.409 --> 02:41:10.579
Fighting for you has been
my life's honor. my lord.

1243
02:41:24.259 --> 02:41:26.970
Open the gates!
Open the gates!

1244
02:41:41.109 --> 02:41:42.778
Here.

1245
02:42:09.137 --> 02:42:10.806
Plague.

1246
02:42:11.473 --> 02:42:14.101
Don't go too close. my king.

1247
02:42:14.851 --> 02:42:17.104
This is the will of the gods.

1248
02:42:17.270 --> 02:42:19.189
They desecrated the temple of Apollo...

1249
02:42:19.731 --> 02:42:22.234
...and Apollo desecrated their flesh.

1250
02:42:22.401 --> 02:42:26.321
They thought they could come here
and sack our city in a day.

1251
02:42:26.488 --> 02:42:30.325
Now look at them.
fleeing across the Aegean.

1252
02:42:33.870 --> 02:42:35.664
What is this?

1253
02:42:35.831 --> 02:42:40.544
An offering to Poseidon. The Greeks
are praying for a safe return home.

1254
02:42:40.710 --> 02:42:43.588
I hope the sea god spits in their offering.

1255
02:42:43.755 --> 02:42:46.425
Lets them all drown
at the bottom of the sea.

1256
02:42:46.591 --> 02:42:50.470
This is a gift. We should take it
to the temple of Poseidon.

1257
02:42:51.513 --> 02:42:53.515
-I think we should burn it.
-Burn it?

1258
02:42:53.682 --> 02:42:55.517
My prince. it's a gift to the gods.

1259
02:42:55.809 --> 02:42:58.019
The prince is right.

1260
02:42:58.186 --> 02:43:01.731
I would burn the whole of Greece
if I had a big enough torch.

1261
02:43:01.898 --> 02:43:05.610
I warn you. good men.
be careful what you insult.

1262
02:43:06.194 --> 02:43:10.365
Our beloved Prince Hector
had sharp words for the gods...

1263
02:43:10.532 --> 02:43:13.660
...and a day later
Achilles' sword out him down.

1264
02:43:13.827 --> 02:43:16.371
Father. burn it.

1265
02:43:17.164 --> 02:43:20.083
Forgive me. my king.
I mean no disrespect...

1266
02:43:20.250 --> 02:43:23.003
...but I don't want to see
any more sons of Troy...

1267
02:43:23.170 --> 02:43:25.714
...incur the gods' wrath.

1268
02:43:27.716 --> 02:43:31.428
I will not watch another son die.

1269
02:44:42.958 --> 02:44:44.501
Look at them.

1270
02:44:46.336 --> 02:44:48.797
You'd think their prince had never died.

1271
02:44:50.966 --> 02:44:53.051
You are their prince now.

1272
02:44:53.802 --> 02:44:55.845
Make your brother proud.

1273
02:50:48.448 --> 02:50:52.493
Let it burn! Let Troy burn!

1274
02:50:52.660 --> 02:50:57.206
Burn it! For Menelaus! Burn it!

1275
02:50:57.457 --> 02:51:02.295
Burn Troy! Burn Troy!

1276
02:51:02.462 --> 02:51:06.090
I promised you. brother!
I promised you!

1277
02:51:06.257 --> 02:51:09.636
Burn it! Burn it for Menelaus!

1278
02:51:54.180 --> 02:51:55.974
Briseis. Where is she?

1279
02:51:56.140 --> 02:51:58.393
-Where?
-I don't know.

1280
02:51:58.559 --> 02:52:00.395
Please. I have a son.

1281
02:52:00.770 --> 02:52:03.231
Then get him out of Troy.

1282
02:52:09.821 --> 02:52:11.155
Briseis!

1283
02:52:15.326 --> 02:52:18.413
Paris! Andromache!

1284
02:52:19.831 --> 02:52:21.666
Helen. We must go.

1285
02:52:21.833 --> 02:52:23.835
-Where?
-I'll show you. Now. Hurry.

1286
02:52:24.002 --> 02:52:25.420
Paris. Paris.

1287
02:52:25.586 --> 02:52:28.297
It's a long way. Quick. We must go now.

1288
02:52:28.464 --> 02:52:30.091
Briseis!

1289
02:52:33.261 --> 02:52:35.054
Paris!

1290
02:52:41.769 --> 02:52:43.104
It's a long way. Quick.

1291
02:52:43.271 --> 02:52:45.606
Hurry. There's a tunnel.

1292
02:52:47.817 --> 02:52:49.402
-Come.
-I stay.

1293
02:52:49.569 --> 02:52:51.821
-No.
-My father will never abandon the city.

1294
02:52:51.988 --> 02:52:53.072
I can't leave him.

1295
02:52:53.281 --> 02:52:56.784
The city is dead.
They're burning it to the ground.

1296
02:52:58.828 --> 02:53:00.788
-What's your name?
-Aeneas.

1297
02:53:00.955 --> 02:53:03.958
-Do you know how to use a sword?
-Yes.

1298
02:53:04.125 --> 02:53:06.085
The sword of Troy.

1299
02:53:06.252 --> 02:53:09.797
As long as it's in the hands of a Trojan.
our people have a future.

1300
02:53:09.964 --> 02:53:12.508
Protect them. Aeneas.
Find them a new home.

1301
02:53:12.759 --> 02:53:15.136
-I Will.
-Hurry. Quick.

1302
02:53:15.303 --> 02:53:17.722
Paris. Paris. Briseis wasn't in her room.

1303
02:53:17.889 --> 02:53:19.390
I'll find her.

1304
02:53:21.809 --> 02:53:23.478
Go.

1305
02:53:24.312 --> 02:53:26.022
-I'll stay with you.
-Go.

1306
02:53:26.189 --> 02:53:27.398
Please don't leave me.

1307
02:53:27.565 --> 02:53:29.734
-How could you love me if I ran now?
-Please.

1308
02:53:29.901 --> 02:53:34.197
We will be together again. in this world
or the next. We will be together.

1309
02:53:40.995 --> 02:53:42.622
Go.

1310
02:53:46.209 --> 02:53:48.377
To the gate!

1311
02:53:48.669 --> 02:53:50.379
Forward!

1312
02:54:07.980 --> 02:54:09.524
Follow me!

1313
02:54:11.776 --> 02:54:13.111
Into line!

1314
02:54:15.113 --> 02:54:17.115
Soldiers of Troy...

1315
02:54:17.406 --> 02:54:19.700
...you men are warriors!

1316
02:54:19.867 --> 02:54:22.537
To lead you has been my honor!

1317
02:54:23.996 --> 02:54:25.540
My prince!

1318
02:54:27.250 --> 02:54:29.210
The boatman waits for us.

1319
02:54:29.460 --> 02:54:33.840
I say we make him wait a little longer!

1320
02:54:56.279 --> 02:54:59.448
No one. Spare no one.

1321
02:55:09.917 --> 02:55:11.294
Paris!

1322
02:55:12.086 --> 02:55:14.046
Save yourself.

1323
02:55:44.785 --> 02:55:46.078
Briseis!

1324
02:56:09.018 --> 02:56:12.772
Beware. my friends.
I am a servant of the gods.

1325
02:56:37.713 --> 02:56:42.510
Have you no honor?

1326
02:56:56.607 --> 02:56:59.694
I wanted you alive. old man.

1327
02:57:00.152 --> 02:57:03.072
I wanted you to watch your city burn.

1328
02:57:05.032 --> 02:57:06.826
Please.

1329
02:57:08.202 --> 02:57:10.329
The children.

1330
02:57:12.665 --> 02:57:16.669
Spare the innocents.

1331
02:57:17.420 --> 02:57:19.297
Nobody's innocent.

1332
02:57:20.089 --> 02:57:21.882
Nobody.

1333
02:57:41.902 --> 02:57:44.405
Too late for prayer. priestess.

1334
02:57:53.664 --> 02:57:57.293
I almost lost this war
because of your little romance.

1335
02:57:58.753 --> 02:58:03.132
I want to taste what Achilles tasted.

1336
02:58:18.105 --> 02:58:22.526
You'll be my slave in Mycenae.

1337
02:58:22.693 --> 02:58:28.199
A Trojan priestess scrubbing my floors.

1338
02:58:30.117 --> 02:58:31.452
And at night ....

1339
02:58:45.049 --> 02:58:46.717
Get up!

1340
02:58:49.762 --> 02:58:51.639
Hold her.

1341
02:59:00.022 --> 02:59:01.357
Come with me.

1342
02:59:05.069 --> 02:59:06.612
No!

1343
02:59:14.161 --> 02:59:17.289
Paris!

1344
02:59:22.128 --> 02:59:23.671
No!

1345
02:59:23.838 --> 02:59:25.381
Don't!

1346
02:59:36.934 --> 02:59:39.854
Don't! Please!

1347
02:59:45.359 --> 02:59:47.736
Paris! Don't!

1348
03:00:20.644 --> 03:00:22.062
It's all right.

1349
03:00:23.022 --> 03:00:24.899
It's all right.

1350
03:00:48.005 --> 03:00:49.924
You gave me peace...

1351
03:00:51.759 --> 03:00:53.802
...in a lifetime of war.

1352
03:00:59.099 --> 03:01:00.434
Briseis. come.

1353
03:01:04.772 --> 03:01:06.023
-Go.
-No.

1354
03:01:06.190 --> 03:01:07.441
You must.

1355
03:01:07.608 --> 03:01:09.109
No.

1356
03:01:09.443 --> 03:01:11.111
Troy is falling.

1357
03:01:11.946 --> 03:01:14.323
-Go.
-No.

1358
03:01:14.490 --> 03:01:16.033
Begin anew.

1359
03:01:17.618 --> 03:01:20.871
We must go. I know a way out.

1360
03:01:27.670 --> 03:01:29.004
It's all right.

1361
03:01:31.507 --> 03:01:33.217
Go.

1362
03:01:40.891 --> 03:01:42.184
Go.

1363
03:03:22.409 --> 03:03:24.036
Find peace...

1364
03:03:24.995 --> 03:03:26.497
...my brother.

1365
03:04:37.359 --> 03:04:41.905
If they ever tell my story. let them say...

1366
03:04:42.072 --> 03:04:44.575
...I walked with giants.

1367
03:04:45.242 --> 03:04:48.704
Men rise and fall like the winter wheat...

1368
03:04:48.912 --> 03:04:51.498
...but these names will never die.

1369
03:04:53.417 --> 03:04:56.920
Let them say I lived
in the time of Hector...

1370
03:04:57.087 --> 03:04:59.339
...breaker of horses.

1371
03:04:59.757 --> 03:05:01.675
Let them say...

1372
03:05:01.842 --> 03:05:05.512
...I lived in the time of Achilles.

1372
03:05:06.305 --> 03:06:06.534
